s as much as some once hoped.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some ideas are bigger than others. Some even grow so large that they turn into paradigms, their logic organizing the way we see everything around them. And if you’re uncertain what framework dominates modern life, well, you can take it from the TED conference fixture and Advertising for Humanity founder Dan Pallotta, who put it bluntly enough in a 2011 article for Harvard Business Review: “Brand is everything, and everything is brand.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/06/magazine/06mag-06firstwords-t_CA0/06mag-06firstwords-t_CA0-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/06/magazine/06mag-06firstwords-t_CA0/06mag-06firstwords-t_CA0-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/06/magazine/06mag-06firstwords-t_CA0/06mag-06firstwords-t_CA0-jumbo-v3.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/06/magazine/06mag-06firstwords-t_CA0/06mag-06firstwords-t_CA0-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 1421, 'width': 1421, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/06/magazine/06mag-06firstwords-t_CA0/06mag-06firstwords-t_CA0-thumbStandard-v4.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/06/magazine/06mag-06firstwords-t_CA0/06mag-06firstwords-t_CA0-thumbStandard-v4.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 't