4'}, {'abstract': 'The government in China, long suspicious of internet companies, now sees ambitious titans like Tencent and Alibaba as useful partners.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/02/technology/china-xi-jinping-technology-innovation.html', 'snippet': 'The government in China, long suspicious of internet companies, now sees ambitious titans like Tencent and Alibaba as useful partners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — For the last decade or so, China has defied the truism that only free and open societies can innovate. Even as the Communist Party has kept an iron grip on politics and discourse, the country’s technology industry has grown to rival Silicon Valley’s in sophistication and ambition.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/03/business/03XITECH/merlin_136086774_f6642f25-a833-489f-9edc-945fa49bf4dd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 825, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/03/business/03XITECH/merlin_136086774_f6642f25-a833-489f-9edc-945fa49bf4dd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 825}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/03/business/03XITECH/merlin_136086774_f6642f25-a833-489f-9edc-945fa49bf4dd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 745, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/03/business/03XITECH/merlin_136086774_f6642f25-a833-489f-9edc-945fa49bf4dd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1490, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/03/business/03XITECH/00XITECH-thumbStandard.jpg',