d_count': 939, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eebc4f29-3a6e-5143-a45b-4f0db7ddb23f'}, {'abstract': 'After a decade of backing human rights and reform, the United States is once again backing corruption and strongmen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/02/opinion/cold-war-central-america.html', 'snippet': 'After a decade of backing human rights and reform, the United States is once again backing corruption and strongmen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the last decade, the United States has pursued a foreign policy toward Latin America that married regional security and stability with democracy promotion and economic development. Under the Trump administration, that has begun to change — in an echo of the Cold War, narrowly defined national security concerns increasingly occupy center stage, with fear of invading migrants replacing fear of invading Communists.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/02/opinion/02Isaacs-sub/02Isaacs-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/02/opinion/02Isaacs-sub/02Isaacs-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/02/opinion/02Isaacs-sub/02Isaacs-sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 650, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/02/opinion/02Isaacs-sub/02Isaacs-sub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1301, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/02/opinion/02Isaacs-sub/02Isaacs-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType':