ing through its skin, instead. If it feels threatened, it can shed its tail, which will wriggle for a few minutes, distracting the pursuer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/02/nyregion/the-creepy-magic-of-the-red-backed-salamander.html', 'snippet': 'It does not have lungs, breathing through its skin, instead. If it feels threatened, it can shed its tail, which will wriggle for a few minutes, distracting the pursuer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Red-backed salamanders are slender and distinctly wormlike — which is why their discovery by gardeners raking leaf litter or by children flipping logs can be startling when they skitter off on their four tiny legs. A worm will not raise its alert little head — with its strangely sentient aspect — to meet its finder’s gaze.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/06/nyregion/06nature/merlin_137543895_b2900e16-ceb5-499c-984f-f32122bc8d49-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/06/nyregion/06nature/merlin_137543895_b2900e16-ceb5-499c-984f-f32122bc8d49-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/06/nyregion/06nature/merlin_137543895_b2900e16-ceb5-499c-984f-f32122bc8d49-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/06/nyregion/06nature/merlin_137543895_b2900e16-ceb5-499c-984f-f32122bc8d49-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'imag