pub_date': '2018-05-04T09:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9787b098-af33-513a-956c-82c028b5390e', 'word_count': 375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9787b098-af33-513a-956c-82c028b5390e'}, {'abstract': 'I’ve known my plates longer than I’ve known anyone who is still on the planet. We’ve had good times together.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/04/well/family/family-dishes.html', 'snippet': 'I’ve known my plates longer than I’ve known anyone who is still on the planet. We’ve had good times together.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My father was truly a fool for love. I was born with 10 fingers and 10 toes, a big thing to a man who had 10 fingers but only nine toes, the second and third on his right foot fused together. The doctor thought that the standard “You have a healthy baby girl” would suffice, but no: My father insisted that he run back to the delivery room — run! — to inventory my hands and feet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/01/arts/Sci-Well-Ties-Plates00/merlin_137566779_9e0843ab-6942-4a12-81fb-95aad8e03ace-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 513, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/01/arts/Sci-Well-Ties-Plates00/merlin_137566779_9e0843ab-6942-4a12-81fb-95aad8e03ace-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 513}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/01/arts/Sci-Well-Ties-Plates00/merlin_137566779_9e0843ab-6942-4a12-81fb-95aad8e03ace-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 875, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 't