hemeral materials had a short shelf.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At 85, the painter Dorothea Rockburne is still blazing trails, making art in the unorthodox way she has for seven decades. “There’s stuff in my head,” Ms. Rockburne, an abstractionist with lively, penetrating eyes and a ready smile, recently explained. “It’s really important for me to get it out of my head and into a viewable situation.’’', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/06/arts/06rockburne20/merlin_136792752_595a3ea0-90bc-4e49-931b-30cc4adc74aa-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 840, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/06/arts/06rockburne20/merlin_136792752_595a3ea0-90bc-4e49-931b-30cc4adc74aa-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 840}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/06/arts/06rockburne20/merlin_136792752_595a3ea0-90bc-4e49-931b-30cc4adc74aa-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 732, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/06/arts/06rockburne20/merlin_136792752_595a3ea0-90bc-4e49-931b-30cc4adc74aa-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1463, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/06/arts/06rockburne20/06rockburne20-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/06/arts/06rockburne20/06rockburne20-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/06/arts/06rockburne20/06rockburne20-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dorothea Rockburne’s Ephemeral Art and Enduring Legacy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ephemeral Art, an Enduring Legacy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rockburne, Dorothea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dia: Beacon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-04T09:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phyllis Tuchman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phyllis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tuchman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57d68a5d-6d3d-5102-b330-d1bfb2b2ef50', 'word_count': 1426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57d68a5d-6d3d-5102-b330-d1bfb2b2ef50'}, {'abstract': 'The Vienna-born centenarian has been a fixture at the Grand Bazaar NYC at Columbus Avenue and 77th Street for 30 years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/04/nyregion/how-mathilde-freund-vintage-dealer-spends-her-sundays.html', 'snippet': 'The Vienna-born centenarian has been a fixture at the Grand Bazaar NYC at Columbus Avenue and 77th Street for 30 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the past 30 years, Mathilde Freund, 101, has been selling vintage clothing and antique jewelry at Grand Bazaar NYC at Columbus Avenue and 77th Street. Ms. Freund was born in Vienna in 1916. In 1937, she fled to Paris when the German Army invaded. She came to New York 15 years later, ultimately finding a job as a social worker at what is now Mount Sinai Beth Israel, and then at the French Hospital, until it closed in the late 1970s. That’s when she found her second calling: selling her wares at the flea market. “I never liked a desk job or dealing with papers,” she said. “I like human beings.” Ms. Freund, who takes classes at Fordham University during the week, has lived in the same one-bedroom apartment overlooking Central Park West for 65 years.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/06/nyregion/06ROUTINE13/merlin_137388537_81ca1d3c-a605-4034-801a-77bb4459ae97-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/06/nyregion/06ROUTINE13/merlin_137388537_81ca1d3c-a605-4034-801a-77bb4459ae97-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/06/nyregion/06ROUTINE13/merlin_137388537_81ca1d3c-a605-4034-801a-77bb4459ae97-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/06/nyregion/06ROUTINE13/merlin_137388537_81ca1d3c-a605-4034-801a-77bb4459ae97-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1351, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/06/nyregion/06ROUTINE13/06ROUTINE13-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/06/nyregion/06ROUTINE13/06ROUTINE13-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/06/nyregion/06ROU