riented atmosphere for a firm focus on what matters most: the food. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'While most millennial restaurateurs are populating the Right Bank of Paris with trendy neo-bistros, Baieta is swimming up-Seine. The first restaurant from Julia Sedefdjian, who earned a Michelin star at 21 years old as the chef at Fables de la Fontaine, planted itself on the Rive Gauche in March, foregoing an Instagram-oriented atmosphere for a firm focus on what matters most: the food.       ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/06/travel/06bites1/06bites1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 771, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/06/travel/06bites1/06bites1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 771}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/06/travel/06bites1/06bites1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 797, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/06/travel/06bites1/06bites1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1594, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/06/travel/06bites1/06bites1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/06/travel/06bites1/06bites1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/06/travel/06bites1/06bites1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarg