gain that guilt is a state of being, if not of facts. Like history, it is determined by the winners.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/06/arts/television/billions-recap-not-you-mr-dake.html', 'snippet': 'This week’s episode demonstrated once again that guilt is a state of being, if not of facts. Like history, it is determined by the winners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before we formally open tonight’s recap, here’s a tip, from my critic’s notebook to you. When you get deep into a season of a prestige drama and you see the names of the showrunners pop up under an episode’s “written by” credit? Buckle up. Written by two of the series’s creators, Brian Koppelman and David Levien, and directed with dot-connecting confidence by Michael Morris, this is “Billions” at its best. Ever, I’d say.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/04/arts/06billions-recap/06westworld-recap-slide-15EN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/04/arts/06billions-recap/06westworld-recap-slide-15EN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/04/arts/06billions-recap/06westworld-recap-slide-15EN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/04/arts/06billions-recap/06westworld-recap-slide-15EN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/04/arts/06billions-recap/06westworld-recap-slide-15EN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/04/arts/06billions-recap/06westworld-recap-slide-15EN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/04/arts/06billions-recap/06westworld-recap-slide-15EN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Billions’ Season 3, Episode 7 Recap: Street Punks', 'kicker': 'Billions', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Billions (TV Program)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-07T02:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sean T. Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sean', 'middlename': 'T.', 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/45c80eef-2de9-51a3-9de4-277831e9c7aa', 'word_count': 1469, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45c80eef-2de9-51a3-9de4-277831e9c7aa'}, {'abstract': 'Dolores clearly views some of her fellow hosts as disposable. Is she any better, then, than the humans she seeks to punish?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/06/arts/television/westworld-recap-virtu-e-fortuna.html', 'snippet': 'Dolores clearly views some of her fellow hosts as disposable. Is she any better, then, than the humans she seeks to punish?', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the second episode of the first season of “Westworld,” Lee Sizemore introduced a new narrative called “Odyssey on Red River,” which he described as the “apex” of what Westworld could be, an amplification of the Wild West perversity and ultraviolence that the guests loved. Sizemore was treating Westworld like any other theme park: In order to keep visitors coming back, his answer was to keep building bigger roller coasters. But after soaking in Sizemore’s splashy presentation, Dr. Ford turned it down flat — to his mind, the appeals of Westworld were more abstract than visceral, and the guests’ time in the park spoke more to a deeper existential longing than to the bang-bang action on the surface.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/04/arts/06westworld-recap/06westworld-recap-slide-NJN8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/04/arts/06westworld-recap/06westworld-recap-slide-NJN8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/04/arts/06westworld-recap/06westworld-recap-slide-NJN8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/04/arts/06westworld-recap/06westworld-recap-slide-NJN8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/04/arts/06westworld-recap/06westworld-recap-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/04/arts/06westworld-recap/06westworld-recap-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/04/arts/06westworld-recap/06westworld-recap-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Westworld’ Season 2, Episode 3 Recap: ‘Just Words in My Head’', 'kicker': 'Westworld', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Westworld (TV Program)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-07T02:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Tobias', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tobias', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/825554ad-5909-56e7-b9fd-75803b3e8f1b', 'word_count': 1162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/825554ad-5909-56e7-b9fd-75803b3e8f1b'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Rubio blocked funding to a United Nations-backed corruption panel over concerns it has been “manipulated and used” by a Russian campaign against a family that fled from Russia to Guatemala.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/06/world/americas/guatemala-corruption-marco-rubio.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Rubio blocked funding to a United Nations-backed corruption panel over concerns it has been “manipulated and used” by a Russian campaign against a family that fled from Russia to Guatemala.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MEXICO CITY — President Jimmy Morales of Guatemala has made no secret of his desire to get rid of a United Nations-backed anti-corruption panel that helped bring down his predecessor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/07/wo