s://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/06/pageoneplus/no-corrections-may-7-2018.html', 'snippet': 'No corrections appeared in print on Monday, May 7, 2018.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No corrections appeared in print on Monday, May 7, 2018.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Corrections: May 7, 2018', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2018-05-07T02:55:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Corrections', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0230ff3-5aa0-5266-b3de-e393724b2e62', 'word_count': 74, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0230ff3-5aa0-5266-b3de-e393724b2e62'}, {'abstract': 'This week’s episode gave us Paul Jr.’s back story and, thus, insight into why he resents his father. Let’s just say he has his reasons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/06/arts/television/trust-recap-fx-kodachrome.html', 'snippet': 'This week’s episode gave us Paul Jr.’s back story and, thus, insight into why he resents his father. Let’s just say he has his reasons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'J. Paul Getty was once said to be the richest man in the world, which sounds like a covetable title. At the very least, it should be nice to be his offspring, if not the man himself. But J. Paul Getty had five sons and — according to “Trust” — none were very happy about it. Episode 7 provides a deeper look into why, as we’re finally given the back story for J. Paul Getty II, father to little Paul, whose suffering under Getty Sr. led to despair, addiction and the collapse of his own family.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/04/arts/06trust-recap/06westworld-recap-slide-A96F-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 