fter Hurricane Maria, I was frantically trying to reach a funeral home in San Juan. My dear cousin Alma Otero-Pérez, a free-spirited poet who was my mentor and model growing up on the island, had died overnight at her home for patients with Alzheimer’s. I loved her and the loss pained me, but as her guardian, I needed to focus on medical and legal paperwork and making the necessary funeral arrangements from New York.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/travel/13sanjuan/merlin_133998873_9eff7c2c-2ee9-4078-8cca-f4f70f797230-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/13/travel/13sanjuan/merlin_133998873_9eff7c2c-2ee9-4078-8cca-f4f70f797230-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/travel/13sanjuan/merlin_133998873_9eff7c2c-2ee9-4078-8cca-f4f70f797230-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/travel/13sanjuan/merlin_133998873_9eff7c2c-2ee9-4078-8cca-f4f70f797230-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/travel/13sanjuan/13sanjuan-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/13/travel/13sanjuan/13sanjuan-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/travel/13sanjuan/13sanjuan-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Puerto Rico, Waiting for Power, for Tourists, for the Flowers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Storm,  Still Waiting  In Puerto Rico', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Puerto Rico', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Maria (2017)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Power Failures and Blackouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Juan (Puerto Rico)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'El Yunque (Puerto Rico)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-07T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ded4d13-afc7-55fd-91da-61e78f8de025', 'word_count': 1717, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ded4d13-afc7-55fd-91da-61e78f8de025'}, {'abstract': 'An otherworldly archipelago with wide sand beaches, medieval castles and a disproportionate number of world-class restaurants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/07/t-magazine/scottish-hebrides-guide.html', 'snippet': 'An otherworldly archipelago with wide sand beaches, medieval castles and a disproportionate number of world-class restaurants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Hebridean archipelago, which hugs Scotland’s ragged west coast, comprises over 180 islands which extend out into the North Atlantic, forming the British Isles’ final frontier before Newfoundland. Divided into the Inner Hebrides, a coastal barrier of 79 islands, and the Outer Hebrides, a more far-flung cluster of over 100 islands and rocky skerries, of which only a fraction are inhabited, the area occupies a mythical place in Scottish culture. First settled in the Stone Age, the islands remain wild, heather-carpeted outposts of Celtic and Norse tradition, scattered with ancient croft fields, medieval castles and gray-stone fishing villages. The Callanish Stones, a cruciform arrangement of standing stones on the Isle of Lewis, predate the pyramids of Egypt.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/07/t-magazine/09tmag-hebrides-slide-O11N/09tmag-hebrides-slide-O11N-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/07/t-magazine/09tmag-hebrides-slide-O11N/09tmag-hebrides-slide-O11N-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/07/t-magazine/09tmag-hebrides-slide-O11N/09tmag-hebrides-slide-O11N-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/07/t-magazine/09tmag-hebrides-slide-O11N/09tmag-hebrides-slide-O11N-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/07/t-magazine/09tmag-hebrides-slide-O11N/09tmag-hebrides-slide-O11N-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/07/t-magazine/09tmag-hebrides-slide-O11N/09tmag-hebrides-slide-O11N-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/07/t-magazine/09tmag-hebrides-slide-O11N/09tmag-hebrides-slide-O11N-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where to Stay (and What to Eat) in the Scottish Hebrides', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hebrides Islands (Great Britain)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-07T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michaela Trimble', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michaela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Trimble', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a20a284-6bd5-5c11-8513-af4d9cd2f4de', 'word_count': 1285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a20a284-6bd5-5c11-8513-af4d9cd2f4de'}, {'abstract': 'The St. Regis New York has butlers as an amenity for guests. We arrived ready with requests, from coffee to ironing to cupcakes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/07/travel/hotel-butler-service.html', 'snippet': 'The St. Regis New York has butlers as an amenity for guests. We arrived ready with requests, from coffee to ironing to cupcakes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Can a butler really make a hotel stay that much more extraordinary?', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/travel/13TESTRUN/merlin_137694684_453e0b53-a581-4f3d-9153-98560a12e62b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/13/travel/13TESTRUN/merlin_137694684_453e0b53-a581-4f3d-9153-98560a12e62b-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/travel/13TESTRUN/merlin_137694684_453e0b53-a581-4f3d-9153-98560a12e62b-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/travel/13TESTRUN/merlin_137694684_453e0b53-a581-4f3d-9153-98560a12e62b-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/travel/13TESTRUN/merlin_137694684_453e0b53-a581-4f3d-9153-98560a12e62b-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/13/travel/13TESTRUN/merlin_137694684_453e0b53-a581-4f3d-9153-98560a12e62b-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/travel/13TESTRUN/merlin_137694684_453e0b53-a581-4f3d-9153-98560a12e62b-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hotel Butler Service Is Really Nice. Is It Worth the Price?', 'kicker': 'Test Run', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Butler Did It, Again and Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Regis Hotel (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-07T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c994fa8a-3840-5d59-90e6-c55811e01989', 'word_count': 1373, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c994fa8a-3840-5d59-90e6-c55811e01989'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Powell’s 1937 film “The Edge of the World” tells of the desertion of St. Kilda in the Outer Hebrides. Today, the islands’ beauty remains, as do signs of what once was.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/07/t-magazine/hebrides-scotland-michael-powell.html', 'snippet': 'Michael Powell’s 1937 film “The Edge of the World” tells of the desertion of St. Kilda in the Outer Hebrides. Today, the islands’ beauty remains, as do signs of what once was.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT LOOKS LIKE the Island of the Dead as we approach it, rising like an angled furl of black rock from the steel-gray sea, the dark clouds sitting so low and heavy on its head that one fears they’re permanently positioned there, like an irremovable and burdensome crown. The journey to St. Kilda has not been easy. First, there were three consecutive days of last-minute boat cancellations as I sat in Portree on the Isle of Skye off the west coast of Scotland, around 250 miles northwest of Edinburgh, waiting for favorable weather conditions. They arrive, as if by magic, on the very last day that I can conceivably remain on the island before heading back home to London. Without that last-minute salvation, I would have had to return next summer to get to St. Kilda, which is another (nearly) hundred miles farther west. And the phrase “favorable weather conditions” here means something more obscure than the absence of driving rain. It depends on two things — “wind speed,” which is obvious enough once it’s pointed out, and “sea swell,” a surface state of water that dictates whether a boat can make landing at the bay in Hirta, the main island in the small archipelago of St. Kilda. It rains all morning as I take a taxi to Uig, the port from which boats depart to St. Kilda, and increases in intensity for the first three hours of the four-hour ride.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '118', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/26/t-magazine/26tmag-hebrides-slide-0ZFQ/26tmag-hebrides-slide-0ZFQ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 478, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/26/t-magazine/26tmag-hebrides-slide-0ZFQ/26tmag-hebrides-slide-0ZFQ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 478}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/26/t-magazine/26tmag-hebrides-slide-0ZFQ/26tmag-hebrides-slide-0ZFQ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 816, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/26/t-magazine/26tmag-hebrides-slide-0ZFQ/26tmag-hebrides-slide-0ZFQ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1631, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/26/t-magazine/26tmag-hebrides-slide-0ZFQ/26tmag-hebrides-slide-0ZFQ-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/26/t-magazin