type': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/opinion/sunday/29baker/29baker-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1960, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/opinion/sunday/29baker/29baker-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/29/opinion/sunday/29baker/29baker-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/opinion/sunday/29baker/29baker-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Fates of Those Accused of Sexual Assault', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Fates of Those Accused of Assault', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': '#MeToo Movement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weinstein, Harvey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-07T15:42:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b1d48a6-80d8-5764-899c-b8718eaa5739', 'word_count': 579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b1d48a6-80d8-5764-899c-b8718eaa5739'}, {'abstract': 'In an attempt to take on a nearby Whole Foods, the shop has added an “appetizing” section, started selling beer and wine by the glass and installed an espresso bar.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/07/dining/bedford-cheese-shop-williamsburg-brooklyn.html', 'snippet': 'In an attempt to take on a nearby Whole Foods, the shop has added an “appetizing” section, started selling beer and wine by the glass and installed an espresso bar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bedford Cheese Shop does not stand still. The Williamsburg flagship has moved and been enlarged more than once (a Manhattan branch on Irving Place opened in 2014). Now they’re at it again, driven by the opening of Whole Foods nearby, said Jason Scherr, an owner. They have added an “appetizing” section, the New York term for Jewish Eastern European specialties like smoked and cured fish, which are sold by the pound or on bagel sandwiches. They’ve also enhanced their line of prepared foods, started selling beer and wine on tap, and installed an espresso bar at a central island surrounded by increased seating. “We can’t compete with Whole Foods on groceries so we’re doing more with prepared foods and personal interaction,” Mr. Scherr said: Bedford Cheese Shop, 265 Bedford Avenue (Grand Street), Williamsburg, Brooklyn, 718-599-7588, bedfordcheeseshop.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnerbedford/09burnerbedford-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 359, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnerbedford/09burnerbedford-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 359}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnerbedford/09burnerbedford-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 612, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnerbedford/09burnerbedford-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1224, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnerbedford/09burnerbedford-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnerbedford/09burnerbedford-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnerbedford/09burnerbedford-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bedford Cheese Shop Expands in Order to Compete', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Shop: Bedford Cheese Shop  Brings More to the Table', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Supermarkets and Grocery Stores', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bedford Cheese Shop (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Whole Foods Market Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-07T15:46:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21bfcfe2-dc82-5316-beb5-46816262954a', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21bfcfe2-dc82-5316-beb5-46816262954a'}, {'abstract': 'A new book by two American scholars, Febe Armanios and Bogac Ergene, looks deeply into halal food and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/07/dining/halal-food-book.html', 'snippet': 'A new book by two American scholars, Febe Armanios and Bogac Ergene, looks deeply into halal food and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An understanding of the ideation of halal is probably not something picked up at Halal Guys or some other street-food vendor. It’s more than avoiding pork. This new book by a couple of American scholars covers the subject broadly, beyond just food — the term applies to anything that is lawful or legitimate under Islamic law. The authors address slaughtering methods, ingredients in processed foods, alcohol, the global food trade (halal chickens from Brazil are shipped to the Middle East), food in public settings like schools, the growth in certifying agencies, and how it all relates to the Quran. Differing religious opinions going back more than 1,000 years are represented, as is the modern notion of “halal cuisine” or “haute halal”: “Halal Food: A History” by Febe Armanios and Bogac Ergene (Oxford University Press, $29.95).', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnerhalal/09burnerhalal-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 847, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnerhalal/09burnerhalal-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 847}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnerhalal/09burnerhalal-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 726, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnerhalal/09burnerhalal-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1400, 'width': 992, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnerhalal/09burnerhalal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnerhalal/09burnerhalal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnerhalal/09burnerhalal-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Deeper Understanding of Halal', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Understand: Scholarly Insight Of All Things Halal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Halal Foods and Products', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Halal Food: A History (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-07T15:48:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bd017e2-1979-527d-a93d-9d454ee2e9e5', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bd017e2-1979-527d-a93d-9d454ee2e9e5'}, {'abstract': 'If you didn’t get an invite to the Royal Wedding, you can still raise a flute of British sparkling wine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/07/dining/sparkling-wine-royal-wedding.html', 'snippet': 'If you didn’t get an invite to the Royal Wedding, you can still raise a flute of British sparkling wine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Churchill may have loved his Pol Roger, but in recent years the bubbly that the British have been sipping is increasingly homegrown. It will be poured at Windsor Castle to celebrate the royal newlyweds on May 19. And if you are a devoted crown-watcher, you can fill your flute that morning with “British fizz,” as the English restaurateur Jason Hicks, of Jones Wood Foundry and the Shakespeare in Manhattan, has dubbed it. (He will have viewing breakfasts at his restaurants, for $70 per person.) A few labels are now sold in the United States, among them crisp, well-made Chapel Down and Gusbourne, which has been served at Buckingham Palace: Gusbourne brut reserve 2011, $52.99, wine.com; Gusbourne blanc de blancs 2011, $79.99 and Chapel Down Three Graces 2010, $39.99, Union Square Wines & Spirits, 140 Fourth Avenue (13th Street), unionsquarewines.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnerroyal/merlin_137429355_70a8cb11-16ab-49bb-b6c4-87ba590cf7ba-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnerroyal/merlin_137429355_70a8cb11-16ab-49bb-b6c4-87ba590cf7ba-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnerroyal/merlin_137429355_70a8cb11-16ab-49bb-b6c4-87ba590cf7ba-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnerroyal/merlin_137429355_70a8cb11-16ab-49bb-b6c4-87ba590cf7ba-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnerroyal/09burnerroyal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnerroyal/09burnerroyal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnerroyal/09burnerroyal-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Toast the Royal Couple With British Bubbly', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Toast: Sparkling and Suited  For a Royal Wedding', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harry, Prince of Wales', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Markle, Meghan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-07T15:55:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf77f049-bbc5-5b8d-89c1-fe842c5c072c', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf77f049-bbc5-5b8d-89c1-fe842c5c072c'}, {'abstract': 'Christopher Kimball has joined with the Swiss company Kuhn Rikon to introduce a line of cookware.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/07/dining/wok-christopher-kimball-kuhn-rikon-cookware.html', 'snippet': 'Christopher Kimball has joined with the Swiss company Kuhn Rikon to introduce a line of cookware.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Christopher Kimball, the food expert who left America’s Test Kitchen and later founded Milk Street, a multimedia company focused on cooking instruction, is introducing a line of cookware. He has developed utensils with Kuhn Rikon, a Swiss company. The carbon steel wok caught my eye, and after taking it for a spin on my gas range I can report that it’s worth adding to the kitchen arsenal. Think of it more as a sauté pan. Its flat bottom lets it sit reliably on the burner grate, it’s well-balanced, the handle stays cool and the weight is not a burden. Once you work your way through Mr. Kimball’s protocol for an initial seasoning, cleaning is a breeze: Christopher Kimball for Kuhn Rikon Collection 5-quart covered wok skillet, $69.95; wok tools $18 each, from surlatable.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnerwok/merlin_137429058_87cf993c-4398-479c-ba5f-d7c5b8b486fe-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnerwok/merlin_137429058_87cf993c-4398-479c-ba5f-d7c5b8b486fe-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnerwok/merlin_137429058_87cf993c-4398-479c-ba5f-d7c5b8b486fe-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnerwok/merlin_137429058_87cf993c-4398-479c-ba5f-d7c5b8b486fe-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnerwok/09burnerwok-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnerwok/09burnerwok-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnerwok/09burnerwok-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Wok With Versatility and Comfort', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Sizzle: Serving Up Comfort And Versatility, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cookware', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kimball, Christopher', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kuhn Rikon Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-07T15:57:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54030ca0-a726-50d9-b509-7eae483a4dab', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54030ca0-a726-50d9-b509-7eae483a4dab'}, {'abstract': 'Luke Heimlich is among the best collegiate pitchers and may take Oregon State to the College World Series. He was also convicted of molesting his 6-year-old niece, a crime he says never happened.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/07/sports/luke-heimlich-sex-crime.html', 'snippet': 'Luke Heimlich is among the best collegiate pitchers and may take Oregon State to the College World Series. He was also convicted of molesting his 6-year-old niece, a crime he says never happened.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CORVALLIS, Ore. —  Luke Heimlich, one of the best players in college baseball, and certainly its most controversial, strode to the mound, dusted away a patch of dirt with his cleats and lined up for his first pitch.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/08/sports/08pitcher-web2/merlin_137531232_dbd8105a-2de2-4cb9-a518-3369a86b2cdd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/08/sports/08pitcher-web2/merlin_137531232_dbd8105a-2de2-4cb9-a518-3369a86b2cdd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/08/sports/08pitcher-web2/merlin_137531232_dbd8105a-2de2-4cb9-a518-3369a86b2cdd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/08/sports/08pitcher-web2/merlin_137531232_dbd8105a-2de2-4cb9-a518-3369a86b2cdd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/08/sports/08pitcher-web2/08pitcher-web2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/08/sports/08pitcher-web2/08pitcher-web2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'captio