 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Caviar', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sandwiches', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ingber, Sandy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-07T16:02:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bdb6ffb-add9-5520-9bbf-35e3a4fe36fb', 'word_count': 141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bdb6ffb-add9-5520-9bbf-35e3a4fe36fb'}, {'abstract': 'A 9-year-old planting lima beans helps a community question assumptions, in this family theater work based on a young-adult novel by Paul Fleischman.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/07/theater/seedfolks-review.html', 'snippet': 'A 9-year-old planting lima beans helps a community question assumptions, in this family theater work based on a young-adult novel by Paul Fleischman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It all begins with a 9-year-old Vietnamese immigrant and a handful of lima beans. But what grows from that modest start seems to fill not only a vacant lot in a fictionalized Cleveland, but also the whole of the New Victory Theater and the rapt hearts of its audience.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/08/arts/08seedfolk/merlin_137693832_226efe36-e5b6-487a-9528-33f375da84d6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/08/arts/08seedfolk/merlin_137693832_226efe36-e5b6-487a-9528-33f375da84d6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/08/arts/08seedfolk/merlin_137693832_226efe36-e5b6-487a-9528-33f375da84d6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/08/arts/08seedfolk/merlin_137693832_226efe36-e5b6-487a-9528-33f375da84d6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 1800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/08/arts/08seedfolk/08seedfolk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/08/arts/08seedfolk/08seedfolk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/08/arts/08seedfolk/08seedfolk-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘Seedfolks,’ Harvesting Hope and Humanity in a Community Garden', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Garden Is Sown, And Hope Takes Root', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Victory Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Seedfolks (Play)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Children's Theater Co (Minneapolis, Minn)", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fleischman, Paul', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brosius, Peter C', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parks, Sonja', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-07T16:06:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laurel Graeber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laurel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Graeber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5583c3b-95df-5927-9f1b-57b8b4cdf007', 'word_count': 416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5583c3b-95df-5927-9f1b-57b8b4cdf007'}, {'abstract': 'The French pastry chef Maxime Pouvreau has expanded his business nationwide with his Petit Pot brand.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/07/dining/pot-de-creme-petit-pot.html', 'snippet': 'The French pastry chef Maxime Pouvreau has expanded his business nationwide with his Petit Pot brand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In France it’s not pudding, it’s pot de crème (poe duh KREM). And for the past few years, the French pastry chef Maxime Pouvreau has been making pots de crème in San Francisco in a handful of flavors sold on the West Coast. Now, having recently expanded his business, he is offering them online and in stores from West to East. The brand is Petit Pot in single-serving 3.5-ounce glass jars. Vanilla, salted caramel, lemon curd and intense dark chocolate are the flavors. There is also creamy rice pudding, riz au lait, and a nondairy version, riz au lait coco. All are kosher: Petit Pot, $39.99 for eight including shipping, petitpot.com, about $3.50 a jar retail.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnercreme/09burnercreme-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 325, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnercreme/09burnercreme-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 325}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnercreme/09burnercreme-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 555, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnercreme/09burnercreme-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1109, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnercreme/09burnercreme-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnercreme/09burnercreme-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/dining/09burnercreme/09burnercreme-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dress Up Brown-Bag Dessert with Pot de Crème', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Spoon: Portable Puddings From a French Chef', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pudding', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Desserts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pouvreau, Maxime', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-07T16:06:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e54f2e0-2400-5017-8735-bff177657424', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e54f2e0-2400-5017-8735-bff177657424'}, {'abstract': 'As problems mount with lethal injection, Alabama, Mississippi and Oklahoma are developing protocols for using nitrogen to carry out the death penalty. Little science exists about the method.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/07/health/death-penalty-nitrogen-executions.html', 'snippet': 'As problems mount with lethal injection, Alabama, Mississippi and Oklahoma are developing protocols for using nitrogen to carry out the death penalty. Little science exists about the method.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hamstrung by troubles with lethal injection — gruesomely botched attempts, legal battles and growing difficulty obtaining the drugs — states are looking for alternative ways to carry out the death penalty. High on the list for some is a method that has never been used before: inhaling nitrogen gas.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/08/science/DEATH1/merlin_137800125_46257f17-0acb-4c1b-871c-7d6820ebf5e9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 596, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/08/science/DEATH1/merlin_137800125_46257f17-0acb-4c1b-871c-7d6820ebf5e9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 596}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/08/science/DEATH1/merlin_137800125_46257f17-0acb-4c1b-871c-7d6820ebf5e9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1018, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/08/science/DEATH1/merlin_137800125_462