nation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many have heard of Alan Turing, the mathematician and logician who invented modern computing in 1935. They know Turing, the cryptologist who cracked the Nazi Enigma code, helped win World War II. And they remember Turing as a martyr for gay rights who, after being prosecuted and sentenced to chemical castration, committed suicide by eating an apple laced with cyanide in 1954. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/15/science/05TB-TURING/merlin_137611185_519449c5-f25b-425c-93fe-a3aa31a955be-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 799, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/15/science/05TB-TURING/merlin_137611185_519449c5-f25b-425c-93fe-a3aa31a955be-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 799}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/15/science/05TB-TURING/merlin_137611185_519449c5-f25b-425c-93fe-a3aa31a955be-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 770, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/15/science/05TB-TURING/merlin_137611185_519449c5-f25b-425c-93fe-a3aa31a955be-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1539, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/15/science/05TB-TURING/05TB-TURING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/15/science/05TB-TURING/05TB-TURING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'typ