e': 'organizations', 'value': 'Soogil (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lim, Soogil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-08T17:35:10+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Food', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/ab9c2369-300d-5eeb-8f06-ec34431c68ef', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/ab9c2369-300d-5eeb-8f06-ec34431c68ef'}, {'abstract': 'Soogil’s chef was a sous-chef at Daniel; it shows in his love of foie gras and his soy-braised short rib.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/08/dining/soogil-review-east-village.html', 'snippet': 'Soogil’s chef was a sous-chef at Daniel; it shows in his love of foie gras and his soy-braised short rib.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A little skepticism is in order when you hear about the work history of a chef running a kitchen for the first time. As frequent diners know from sad experience, it is, in fact, possible to cook in an acclaimed restaurant without picking up any of the qualities that it’s acclaimed for. Even when actual skills have been learned, they are not always obvious. Or, occasionally, they’re all too obvious, and you’ll catch somebody in a two-person kitchen trying to replicate dishes originally assembled by a team of 40.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'French Skills Meet Korean Flavors at Soogil in the East Village', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Modern Asian Presented With French Flair', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Soogil (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lim, Soogil', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Eas