Boom for Real’ Is a Beguiling Look at a Teenage Basquiat', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Beguiling Look at a Teenage Artist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Basquiat, Jean-Michel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Boom for Real: The Late Teenage Years of Jean-Michel Basquiat (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Driver, Sara', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-09T11:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Kenny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5a89b83-197f-5b60-b9ab-5c8aa4edacaa', 'word_count': 501, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5a89b83-197f-5b60-b9ab-5c8aa4edacaa'}, {'abstract': 'Annette Bening, Saoirse Ronan and Elisabeth Moss are highlights of Michael Mayer’s adaptation of the durable Chekhov play.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/09/movies/the-seagull-review.html', 'snippet': 'Annette Bening, Saoirse Ronan and Elisabeth Moss are highlights of Michael Mayer’s adaptation of the durable Chekhov play.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Watching Annette Bening as Irina Arkadina in “The Seagull,” Michael Mayer’s adaptation of the durable Anton Chekhov play, you might almost believe that the role was written with her in mind. There is very little Ms. Bening can’t do, but one of the things she does best is play actresses — the title character in “Being Julia,” Gloria Grahame in “Film Stars Don’t Die in Liverpool” and now Chekhov’s diva of the late-19th-century Moscow stage. Irina is charming and silly, imperious and intelligent, tough to the point of cruelty and also exquisitely sensitive. Her brother’s country estate, where nearly all of the drama takes place, is a hive of shifting loyalty, jealousy and desire, dominated by Irina’s grand and difficult personality.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/11/arts/11theseagull/merlin_137696949_7bf69969-3774-4b51-ab85-5e8cb60096d9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 347, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/11/arts/11theseagull/merlin_137696949_7bf69969-3774-4b51-ab85-5e8cb60096d9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 347}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/11/arts/11theseagull/merlin_137696949_7bf69969-3774-4b51-ab85-5e8cb60096d9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 592, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/11/arts/11theseagull/merlin_137696949_7bf69969-3774-4b51-ab85-5e8cb60096d9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1183, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/11/arts/11theseagull/11theseagull-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/11/arts/11theseagull/11theseagull-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/11/arts/11theseagull/11theseagull-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘The Seagull,’ a Great Play, a Great Cast and Yet ...', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It’s Great Chekhov, but the Camera Gets in the Way', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Seagull (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mayer, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bening, Annette', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chekhov, Anton', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ronan, Saoirse', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moss, Elisabeth', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-09T11:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/49f4b7c7-b149-55dc-b8dd-0c5d5bcab1fc', 'word_count': 630, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49f4b7c7-b149-55dc-b8dd-0c5d5bcab1fc'}, {'abstract': 'Coralie Fargeat’s debut feature is a skillful and gory fusion of feminism and exploitation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/09/movies/revenge-review.html', 'snippet': 'Coralie Fargeat’s debut feature is a skillful and gory fusion of feminism and exploitation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Blunt, bloody and stylish almost in spite of itself, “Revenge” is a synthesis of exploitation and feminism, which might strike you as antithetical ideas. The basic plot — a woman collecting payback from the men who have assaulted her — is not exactly new, and it’s a conceit that can be used as an alibi. The way a movie like this often goes is that the audience is invited to revel in the spectacle of sexual violence and also in the violent punishment that follows. Misogyny is indulged so it can be condemned, and vice versa.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/11/arts/11revenge2/11revenge2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 251, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/11/arts/11revenge2/11revenge2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 251}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/11/arts/11revenge2/11revenge2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 428, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/11/arts/11revenge2/11revenge2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 856, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/11/arts/11revenge2/11revenge2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/11/arts/11revenge2/11revenge2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/11/arts/11revenge2/11revenge2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘Revenge,’ the Trophy Turns Hunter', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Trophy Becomes the Hunter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank'