yline': {'original': 'By Ingrid K. Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ingrid', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe96130a-4cd7-566d-8470-5a2daeada934', 'word_count': 1497, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe96130a-4cd7-566d-8470-5a2daeada934'}, {'abstract': 'As the first black actor to star as Billy Bigelow on Broadway, Mr. Henry is changing theater, while a newborn son is changing him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/10/theater/joshua-henry-carousel-billy-bigelow.html', 'snippet': 'As the first black actor to star as Billy Bigelow on Broadway, Mr. Henry is changing theater, while a newborn son is changing him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Samson Peter Henry, his parents’ first child, made his debut on the cusp of spring, at around 9 o’clock one morning this March. For his mother, Cathryn Henry, a postpartum nurse at New York-Presbyterian Hospital, it was a kind of Have Your Child at Work situation.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/arts/13henry10/13henry10-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/13/arts/13henry10/13henry10-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/arts/13henry10/13henry10-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/arts/13henry10/13henry10-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo',