28580e1-0bb9-5211-a064-d3444ed8993c'}, {'abstract': 'Readers count the ways they love and loathe turning 40, and answer the question: Do grown-ups really exist?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/10/opinion/what-its-like-to-turn-40.html', 'snippet': 'Readers count the ways they love and loathe turning 40, and answer the question: Do grown-ups really exist?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a recent essay, Pamela Druckerman reflected on the sudden shift of being 40. People addressed her differently, expected punctuality and looked to her as the responsible adult in the room. She asked, “What is a grown-up anyway? Do they really exist?” Many grown-ups responded and enumerated the wonderful — and not so wonderful — things about aging. Below are some of those comments, edited for length and clarity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/opinion/sunday/09druckermancomments/09druckermancomments-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 638, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/09/opinion/sunday/09druckermancomments/09druckermancomments-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 638}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/opinion/sunday/09druckermancomments/09druckermancomments-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 963, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/opinion/sunday/09druckermancomments/09druckermancomments-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1926, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/opinion/sunday/09druckermancomments/09druckermancomments-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/09/opinion/sunday/09druckermancomments/09druckermancomments-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/opinion/sunday/09druckermancomments/09druckermancomments-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'You Know You’re 40 When...', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birthdays', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-10T09:45:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fb19e33-7f87-5b41-9110-27767fc53a33', 'word_count': 1488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fb19e33-7f87-5b41-9110-27767fc53a33'}, {'abstract': 'It is educated voters who are making politics more polarized.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/10/opinion/democrats-partisanship-identity-politics.html', 'snippet': 'It is educated voters who are making politics more polarized.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Should taxes on households making $250,000 or more a year be raised? When you ask Democrats this question, you get a very interesting answer: Those on the bottom of the income distribution appear to want lower taxes on high earners than those on the top do.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/10/opinion/10edsallWeb/merlin_114167