/article/7d4f1fe4-d635-59a7-a544-2b9f0f10bfd5'}, {'abstract': 'His administration has come down on opposite sides of arguments about whether to enact internet sales taxes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/10/opinion/is-trumps-tax-incoherence-just-a-way-to-hurt-amazon.html', 'snippet': 'His administration has come down on opposite sides of arguments about whether to enact internet sales taxes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For months, the Trump administration has rightfully been trying to thwart attempts by some European governments to impose a new corporate “digital tax” on American high-tech giants. This campaign to block internet-inspired extraterritorial taxation — taxation of income earned outside of a jurisdiction — is strongly supported by the American business community. But the White House, in an odd twist that turns its European Union digital tax arguments upside down, just argued before the Supreme Court that the same kind of extraterritorial taxation is acceptable when carried out by American states on retail sales on the internet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/10/opinion/10derugy/merlin_136980681_6bcd0fb5-f999-4f09-9b52-6591d735ea41-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/10/opinion/10derugy/merlin_136980681_6bcd0fb5-f999-4f09-9b52-6591d735ea41-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/10/opinion/10derugy/merlin_136980681_6bcd0fb5-f999-4f09-9b52-6591d735ea41-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/10/opinion/10derugy/merlin_136980681_6bcd0fb5-f99