g-with-2300-miles-to-work.html', 'snippet': 'Two Tajik friends deal with the dilemma of remaining at home with few job prospects, or heading to Russia for possible work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The filmmaker Tim Brown and the illustrator George Butler teamed up to capture one of the world’s largest migrations in “2,300 Miles to Work,” a ten-minute film that also touches on themes of survival, the bonds of friendship and family. It profiles two young Tajiks who encounter the same dilemma — to remain at home with dwindling work prospects or to head to Russia for possible work.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Teaching With: ‘2,300 Miles to Work’', 'kicker': 'Film Club', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2018-05-10T19:37:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caroline Crosson Gilpin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caroline', 'middlename': 'Crosson', 'lastname': 'Gilpin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/924eda6a-498b-519a-94e9-0e1bb9270def', 'word_count': 653, 'uri': 'nyt://article/924eda6a-498b-519a-94e9-0e1bb9270def'}, {'abstract': 'A reader recalls Mother’s Day through the years from her perspective as a gay mother.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/10/opinion/mothers-day.html', 'snippet': 'A reader recalls Mother’s Day through the years from her perspective as a gay mother.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/07/opinion/07renklWeb/07renklWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLar