urors Are Silenced', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Jurors Are Silenced', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jury System', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oregon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Advocate, The (Baton Rouge, La, Newspaper)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-10T23:12:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c1412e0-cc7a-50e4-aed9-a80ebf883321', 'word_count': 855, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c1412e0-cc7a-50e4-aed9-a80ebf883321'}, {'abstract': 'Moms can be so annoying. But where would we be without them?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/10/opinion/mothers-day-2018.html', 'snippet': 'Moms can be so annoying. But where would we be without them?', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I was in my freewheeling 20s, the conversation over drinks with friends once turned to our mothers — and how they drove us nuts. I laughed at my friends’ gripes and shared my own, but I also wondered, “Why would I ever want to become this annoying person in someone’s life?” Nonetheless, I did have a child within a decade of that conversation. It didn’t take me long to realize that 1) I was in way over my head and I’d better call my mom, and 2) if my kid didn’t sometimes find me annoying, I probably wasn’t doing it right.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/05/03/sunday-review/03MOTHERsub/03MOTHERsub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/05/03/sunday-review/03MOTHERsub/03MOTHERsub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/05/03/sunday-review/03MOTHERsub/03MOTHERsub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/05/03/sunday-review/03MOTHERsub/03MOTHERsub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/05/03/sunday-review/03MOTHERsub/03MOTHERsub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/05/03/sunday-review/03MOTHERsub/03MOTHERsub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/05/03/sunday-review/03MOTHERsub/03MOTHERsub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Hand That Rocks and Rules', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Mother's Day", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-10T23:18:34+00