-snapping rhetorical turn has opened the president to criticism that he has been too quick to embrace a brutal leader as a worthy negotiating partner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/10/us/politics/trump-kim-jong-un-language.html', 'snippet': 'The head-snapping rhetorical turn has opened the president to criticism that he has been too quick to embrace a brutal leader as a worthy negotiating partner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Less than a year ago, President Trump was savaging Kim Jong-un, the North Korean leader, as a “madman” and murderer of his own people, branding him “Little Rocket Man” for his nuclear testing exploits and poking fun at his portly stature.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/12/us/politics/11dc-trumpwords-1/merlin_135221355_c7fb864d-755d-4ba3-9079-6f4453e35121-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 362, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/12/us/politics/11dc-trumpwords-1/merlin_135221355_c7fb864d-755d-4ba3-9079-6f4453e35121-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 362}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/12/us/politics/11dc-trumpwords-1/merlin_135221355_c7fb864d-755d-4ba3-9079-6f4453e35121-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 618, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/12/us/politics/11dc-trumpwords-1/merlin_135221355_c7fb864d-755d-4ba3-9079-6f4453e35121-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1235, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/12/us/politics/11dc-trumpwords-