cd9cd86e-407a-5e45-9213-ff1e00c015c6', 'word_count': 1312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd9cd86e-407a-5e45-9213-ff1e00c015c6'}, {'abstract': 'From critical reviews and artist profiles to annotated playlists and music-inspired poetry, we suggest ideas for integrating music into your curriculum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/10/learning/lesson-plans/nine-teaching-ideas-for-using-music-to-inspire-student-writing.html', 'snippet': 'From critical reviews and artist profiles to annotated playlists and music-inspired poetry, we suggest ideas for integrating music into your curriculum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some of the greatest written works of our time have been inspired by music. Walt Whitman conceived of and wrote “Leaves of Grass” while listening to opera. Alice Walker, Langston Hughes, Ntozake Shange and Ralph Ellison were all moved by spirituals, jazz and blues. And Lin-Manuel Miranda’s rap musical “Hamilton” was born of his love of hip-hop. These writers understood what many educational researchers know — that music opens up pathways to creative thinking, sharpens our ability to listen and helps us weave together disparate ideas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/12/magazine/12music5-kelela2-LNMusic/12music5-kelela2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/12/magazine/12music5-kelela2-LNMusic/12music5-kelela2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/12/magazine/12music5-kelela2-LNMusic/12music5-kelela2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 615, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/12/magazine/12music5-kelela2-LNMusic/12music5-kelela2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1229, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/12/magazine/12music5-kelela2-LNMusic/12music5-kelela2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/12/magazine/12music5-kelela2-LNMusic/12music5-kelela2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/12/magazine/12music5-kelela2-LNMusic/12music5-kelela2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nine Teaching Ideas for Using Music to Inspire Student Writing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2018-05-11T00:15:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'subsection_name': 'Lesson Plans', 'byline': {'original': 'By Natalie Proulx', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Natalie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Proulx', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3bf3f32a-85a8-5a06-9af1-74eedb7db562', 'word_count': 3600, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3bf3f32a-85a8-5a06-9af1-74eedb7db562'}, {'abstract': 'The three American prisoners released by North Korea this week may find that coming home from internment is not without its own struggles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/10/us/north-korea-detained.html', 'snippet': 'The three American prisoners released by North Korea this week may find that coming home from internment is not without its own struggles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For Euna Lee, certain moments of her return from months of confinement in North Korea in the summer of 2009 were marked by what she recalls as “utter joy.” The tearful reunion with her husband and 4-year-old daughter; savoring a meal at a favorite local restaurant in Los Angeles.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/11/us/11detainees2/merlin_137715885_0a471b61-4da4-40ad-a707-5440bb226753-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/11/us/11detainees2/merlin_137715885_0a471b61-4da4-40ad-a707-5440bb226753-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/11/us/11detainees2/merlin_137715885_0a471b61-4da4-40ad-a707-5440bb226753-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/11/us/11detainees2/merlin_137715885_0a471b61-4da4-40ad-a707-5440bb226753-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/11/us/11detainees2/merlin_137715885_0a471b61-4da4-40ad-a707-5440bb226753-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/11/us/11detainees2/merlin_137715885_0a471b61-4da4-40ad-a707-5440bb226753-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url'