ner used found objects — and yes, sequins — to dress an eye-popping array of singing, dancing sea creatures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To bring to life the wackadoo cartoon world of Bikini Bottom in “SpongeBob SquarePants: The Broadway Musical,” the designer David Zinn went for a bright, found-object aesthetic that mixes “Pee-wee’s Playhouse,” Etsy craft, classic MGM musicals and acid-house clubland. In this world, a mermaid’s tail is festooned with rubber gloves.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/arts/13spongecostume1/13spongecostume1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 601, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/13/arts/13spongecostume1/13spongecostume1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 601}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/arts/13spongecostume1/13spongecostume1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1023, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/arts/13spongecostume1/13spongecostume1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2045, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/arts/13spongecostume1/13spongecostume1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/13/arts/13spongecostume1/13spongecostume1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/arts/13spongecostume1/13spong