https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/11/magazine/poem-examples-of-justice.html', 'snippet': 'Selected by Terrance Hayes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The distance between poet and poem is wonderfully, sometimes perilously, elastic. This shrewd poem’s particularness creates an intimacy that feels both personal and social. I wouldn’t call the details universal, I would call them recognizable. We may not know who Kathleen is, for example, but we know what it means to feel lost. The speaker (the poet?) addresses us like an old friend with an air that is both forsaken and resilient. Selected by Terrance Hayes', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/magazine/13Poem_01/13Poem_01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 422, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/13/magazine/13Poem_01/13Poem_01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 422}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/magazine/13Poem_01/13Poem_01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 705, 'width': 1003, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/magazine/13Poem_01/13Poem_01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 705, 'width': 1003, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/magazine/13Poem_01/13Poem_01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/13/magazine/13Poem_01/13Poem_01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None,