 {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Najib Razak', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ibrahim, Anwar', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-12T18:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4e10398-9c7b-553a-95e8-2804e45d2f31', 'word_count': 465, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4e10398-9c7b-553a-95e8-2804e45d2f31'}, {'abstract': 'I apologize for bumming other people out on a motherless Mother’s Day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/12/opinion/sunday/im-so-sorry-for-my-loss.html', 'snippet': 'I apologize for bumming other people out on a motherless Mother’s Day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is my ninth motherless Mother’s Day, and while I still feel a little that people who take their mom out to brunch to celebrate are bragging, I’d like to assure you all that I’m fine.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/opinion/sunday/13cella/13cella-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 521, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/13/opinion/sunday/13cella/13cella-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 521}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/opinion/sunday/13cella/13cella-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 889, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/opinion/sunday/13cella/13cella-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1778, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/opinion/sunday/13cella/13cella-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/13/opinion/sunday/13cella/13cella-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/opinion/sunday/13cella/13cella-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I’m So Sorry for My Loss', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I’m So Sorry for My Loss', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Mother's Day", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-12T18:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Cella', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cella', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3792dcfc-b332-55b7-886f-f053976f5f89', 'word_count': 753, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3792dcfc-b332-55b7-886f-f053976f5f89'}, {'abstract': 'I’ve spent a lifetime trying to make a perfect flatbread — a doomed struggle that always makes me think of other failures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/12/opinion/sunday/a-man-and-his-roti.html', 'snippet': 'I’ve spent a lifetime trying to make a perfect flatbread — a doomed struggle that always makes me think of other failures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few years ago, I saw an ad on Pakistani TV that made me, and many others, cringe. In it, a little girl is shown kneading a little ball of dough and making a roti, and her mother announces, with a drum roll, to a jubilant family, “Choti ki pehli gol roti!” (“The little girl’s first round flat bread!”) I despaired at our homegrown capitalists’ attempt to turn girls into kitchen slaves at a time when women in Pakistan were beginning to fly fighter jets and run the foreign ministry.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/opinion/sunday/13hanif/13hanif-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 346, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/13/opinion/sunday/13hanif/13hanif-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 346}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/opinion/sunday/13hanif/13hanif-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 590, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/opinion/sunday/13hanif/13hanif-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1180, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/opinion/sunday/13hanif/13hanif-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/13/opinion/sunday/13hanif/13hanif-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/opinion/sunday/13hanif/13hanif-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Man and His Roti', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Man and His Roti', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bread', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Punjab (Pakistan)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-12T18:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mohammed Hanif', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mohammed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hanif', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a37bc74-bc26-50bf-99ea-b8725f935bed', 'word_count': 1129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a37bc74-bc26-50bf-99ea-b8725f935bed'}, {'abstract': 'There is a dimension beyond that known to man, between the summit of nonsense and the pit of implausibility; it’s a place we call the Trump Zone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/12/opinion/sunday/donald-trump-presidency-maureen-dowd.html', 'snippet': 'There is a dimension beyond that known to man, between the summit of nonsense and the pit of implausibility; it’s a place we call the Trump Zone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Once I would have rolled my eyes at a “Homeland” season in which the Russians deftly maneuvered to control whether a Democratic woman, an increasingly paranoid former junior senator from New York, would occupy the Oval Office.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 