pg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/02/24/dining/24KITCH/24KITCH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/02/24/dining/24KITCH/24KITCH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/02/24/dining/24KITCH/24KITCH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/02/24/dining/24KITCH/24KITCH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/02/24/dining/24KITCH/24KITCH-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Oatmeal! Oatmeal! Oatmeal!', 'kicker': 'What to Cook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-14T14:30:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a25af1c6-2fb4-5c51-be48-be0c5d0d0127', 'word_count': 563, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a25af1c6-2fb4-5c51-be48-be0c5d0d0127'}, {'abstract': 'As discussions about how a man should behave continue, visual culture has already provided a solution to what a man might look like.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/14/t-magazine/age-of-the-twink.html', 'snippet': 'As discussions about how a man should behave continue, visual culture has already provided a solution to what a man might look like.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a scene in “Call Me by Your Name” that I can’t get out of my head. (No, not that one.) It happens near the beginning of Luca Guadagnino’s gay odyssey, when Armie Hammer’s character, Oliver, sweaty from volleyball, pauses to steal a drink from Elio, played by Timothée Chalamet. Sensing Elio’s nervousness, Oliver begins to massage his shoulder. This is memorable not because we’re watching two straight actors perform a pas de deux of muted gay desire, but rather because of their difference in size. Hammer, 31, is 6-foot-5, with broad shoulders and body hair. Chalamet, 22, is five inches shorter, naturally smooth, with a pronounced clavicle and a concave torso. By gay male standards, he’s the ultimate twink.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/30/t-magazine/30tmag-ppt-slide-YD28/30tmag-ppt-slide-YD28-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 361, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/30/t-magazine/30tmag-ppt-slide-YD28/30tmag-ppt-slide-YD28-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 361}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/30/t-magazine/30tmag-ppt-slide-YD28/30tmag-ppt-slide-YD28-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 616, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/30/t-magazine/30tmag-ppt-slide-YD28/30tmag-ppt-slide-YD28-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 984, 'width': 1637, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/30/t-magazine/30tmag-ppt-slide-YD28/30tmag-ppt-slide-YD28-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/30/t-magazine/30tmag-ppt-slide-YD28/30tmag-ppt-slide-YD28-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/30/t-magazine/30tmag-ppt-slide-YD28/30tmag-ppt-slide-YD28-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Welcome to the Age of the Twink', 'kicker': 'Notes on the Culture', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Age of the Twink', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Years & Years (Music Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alexander, Olly', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chalamet, Timothee (1995- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sivan, Troye (1995- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-14T14:45:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Haramis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haramis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/712f683e-7e7d-54ae-8548-ee3608fee0ae', 'word_count': 609, 'uri': 'nyt://article/712f683e-7e7d-54ae-8548-ee3608fee0ae'}, {'abstract': 'A buyer’s question illustrates the importance of due diligence in New York State.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/14/realestate/who-is-responsible-for-illegal-renovations.html', 'snippet': 'A buyer’s question illustrates the importance of due diligence in New York State.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q: After I purchased a Brooklyn condo, I began to suspect that renovations made by the previous owner were illegal. I am concerned that if I try to renovate and file permits with the Department of Buildings, the city will make me rip out the work the previous owner did. When I purchased the unit, the seller did not say anything about  renovations. How do I legalize the work? And who should be held liable for what I consider a fraudulent sale? The seller? My lawyer?', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/realestate/13ASKNADIAPILLON/13ASK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 118, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/13/realestate/13ASKNADIAPILLON/13ASK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 118}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/realestate/13ASKNADIAPILLON/13ASK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 201, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/realestate/13ASKNADIAPILLON/13ASK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 1680, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/13/realestate/13ASKNADIAPILLON/13ASKNAD