uri': 'nyt://article/7ad28a91-37e0-5774-95ac-98f910d3a1b4'}, {'abstract': 'The 29-year-old Zuza Mengham has become known for confection-colored, craggy tabletop pieces.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/14/t-magazine/design/zuza-mengham-sculpture.html', 'snippet': 'The 29-year-old Zuza Mengham has become known for confection-colored, craggy tabletop pieces.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Informally arranged along the windowsill of Zuza Mengham’s light-filled South London studio is a small collection of crystals and natural stones, from smoky quartz to Himalayan salt. The 29-year-old artist grew up in a new-age-leaning household in Cambridge, England, and is not immune to the sort of thinking you might be more likely to find in L.A. “It never hurts to have a bit of positive chi,” she says. These objects, however, are more significant than they might seem. Over the past few years, Mengham, who ', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/30/t-magazine/30tmag-ppt-slide-1X57/30tmag-ppt-slide-1X57-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/30/t-magazine/30tmag-ppt-slide-1X57/30tmag-ppt-slide-1X57-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/30/t-magazine/30tmag-ppt-slide-1X57/30tmag-ppt-slide-1X57-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/30/t-magazine/30tmag-ppt-slide-1X57/30tmag-ppt-slide-1X57-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 