ersons', 'value': 'Williams, Serena', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hair', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-15T09:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bee Shapiro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bee', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shapiro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b62bf2cc-46a8-5b83-adb3-bb07562e035e', 'word_count': 1094, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b62bf2cc-46a8-5b83-adb3-bb07562e035e'}, {'abstract': 'It’s more than just a memoir: It’s logistically stupefying, touching and absolutely packed with choice late-’80s gossip.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/15/magazine/letter-of-recommendation-drew-barrymores-little-girl-lost.html', 'snippet': 'It’s more than just a memoir: It’s logistically stupefying, touching and absolutely packed with choice late-’80s gossip.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Drew Barrymore had her first cigarette when she was 9. Within three years, she would drink her first beer, smoke her first bowl and do her first bump of coke. Soon she was regularly going to a nightclub in Silverlake, a spot favored by Jack Nicholson and Madonna and run by a family friend. Barrymore and her young pals had a routine: They would go up to the balcony, rip cigs and keep watch for drinks to swipe down below. “A few times we passed out up there, slept for several hours and woke up with monumental headaches,” Barrymore would later write, “a combination of the alcohol and lying with our ears right beside the speakers.” It was 1990 when she published those words, and she was 14, having already lived long and hard enough to write a rehab memoir, “Little Girl Lost.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/20/magazine/20LOR-copy/20LOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 437, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/20/magazine/20LOR-copy/20LOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 437}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/20/magazine/20LOR-copy/20LOR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/20/magazine/20LOR-copy/20LOR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1491, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/20/magazine/20LOR-copy/20LOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/20/magazine/20LOR-copy/20LOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/20/magazine/20LOR-copy/20LOR-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Letter of Recommendation: Drew Barrymore’s ‘Little Girl Lost’', 'kicker': 'Letter of Recommendation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Drew Barrymore’s ‘Little Girl Lost’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barrymore, Drew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Addiction (Psychology)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-15T09:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amos Barshad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amos', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barshad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc4b47d7-6cb8-502b-861f-40cb243e9b63', 'word_count': 944, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc4b47d7-6cb8-502b-861f-40cb243e9b63'}, {'abstract': 'A spicy, crunchy Indian fish fry honors a grandmother’s recipe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/15/magazine/a-spicy-crunchy-indian-fish-fry-the-way-her-grandmother-liked-it.html', 'snippet': 'A spicy, crunchy Indian fish fry honors a grandmother’s recipe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Archana Pidathala wrote code, not recipes. And at first, the phrases she read in her grandmother’s cookbook, “Vanita Vantakalu,” published in 1974, made no sense at all. Temper the spices? Pidathala wondered, looking for more information, finding none. How did you go about tempering the spices? ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/20/magazine/20Eat-copy/20Eat-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/20/magazine/20Eat-copy/20Eat-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/201