ourney Into Night.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/16/theater/lesley-manville-long-days-journey-into-night.html', 'snippet': 'England’s hardest-working actress finally gets her star moment in America, playing Mary Tyrone in “Long Day’s Journey Into Night.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mary Tyrone casts a long shadow over “Long Day’s Journey Into Night” while she’s onstage, and while she’s not. For much of the second act, this morphine-addicted mother haunts her husband and sons with her absence. They know that once she disappears up the stairs of their ramshackle summerhouse, she is finding a vein, getting a fix and slipping away. Meanwhile, as soon as Mary steps offstage, the actress Lesley Manville has shaken off the character and started taking care of business. She spends her long break, before returning for Mary’s final dope-fueled monologue, getting her own life in order: taking a shower, doing a bit of sewing, answering emails.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/20/arts/20MANVILLE1-copy/20MANVILLE1-copy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/20/arts/20MANVILLE1-copy/20MANVILLE1-copy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/20/arts/20MANVILLE1-copy/20MANVILLE1-copy-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1023, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/20/arts/20MANVILLE1-copy/20MANVILLE1-copy-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2047, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'cap