y', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Gorce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e025d15-17af-5980-b008-7eee55d5ff3f', 'word_count': 2009, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e025d15-17af-5980-b008-7eee55d5ff3f'}, {'abstract': 'She experienced sharp pain in her gut before, but it always dissipated. This time the stabbing feeling would not go away.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/16/magazine/why-did-the-young-womans-heartburn-keep-getting-worse.html', 'snippet': 'She experienced sharp pain in her gut before, but it always dissipated. This time the stabbing feeling would not go away.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 26-year-old woman lay in her bedroom with the curtains closed and tried not to move. Any shift at all seemed to worsen the nausea and the knifelike pain just below her rib cage. The woman’s mother was surprised to find her in bed. She put her hand on her daughter’s forehead. She was hot, feverish. Have you had anything to eat today, her mother asked. Her daughter shook her head. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/20/magazine/20mag-diagnosis-image1-Promo/20mag-diagnosis-image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 552, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/20/magazine/20mag-diagnosis-image1-Promo/20mag-diagnosis-image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 552}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/20/magazine/20mag-diagnosis-image1-Promo/20mag-diagnosis-image1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 942, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/20/magazine/20mag-diagnosis-image1-Promo/20mag-diagnosis-image1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1884, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/20/magazine/20mag-diagnosis-image1-Promo/20mag-diagnosis-image1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/20/magazine/20mag-diagnosis-image1-Promo/20mag-diagnosis-image1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/20/magazine/20mag-diagnosis-image1-Promo/20mag-diagnosis-image1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Did the Young Woman’s Heartburn Keep Getting Worse?', 'kicker': 'Diagnosis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Crohn's Disease", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Heartburn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-16T09:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Sanders, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sanders', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fa30838-3e0a-5257-8c1a-ba5da276e376', 'word_count': 1399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fa30838-3e0a-5257-8c1a-ba5da276e376'}, {'abstract': 'Tilt your chin toward the sky. For buoyancy, arch your back and keep your lungs full of air.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/16/magazine/how-to-float.html', 'snippet': 'Tilt your chin toward the sky. For buoyancy, arch your back and keep your lungs full of air.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Let your head drop back in the water,” says Bill Durden, who was 60 when he spent 20 hours alone and adrift after falling from his boat and watching it motor away empty from a fishing spot some 30 miles offshore in the Gulf of Mexico. Even if the circumstances are harrowing, lie back and try to relax. Tilt your chin toward the sky and let your head and ears go under, keeping just your nose and eyes exposed. “If you try to hold your head up, you’ll get tired fast,” Durden says.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/20/magazine/20Tip-01/20Tip-01-articleLarge.png', 'height': 506, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/20/magazine/20Tip-01/20Tip-01-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 506}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/20/magazine/20Tip-01/20Tip-01-jumbo.png', 'height': 863, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/20/magazine/20Tip-01/20Tip-01-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1726, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/20/magazine/20Tip-01/20Tip-01-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/20/magazine/20Tip-01/20Tip-01-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'typ