t://article/c2b4391a-77e4-5e1b-834b-cb2bc33123c9', 'word_count': 441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2b4391a-77e4-5e1b-834b-cb2bc33123c9'}, {'abstract': 'As restaurants helmed by queer female couples thrive in American cities, so too does a new paradigm for less brutal, more collaborative, professional cooking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/16/t-magazine/food/female-chefs-rita-sodi-jody-williams-erika-nakamura.html', 'snippet': 'As restaurants helmed by queer female couples thrive in American cities, so too does a new paradigm for less brutal, more collaborative, professional cooking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a cold February morning, Erika Nakamura, 37, studious in gold wire-rim glasses, quietly shaved panels of beef with a blade curved like a scimitar. Standing close, hair tucked under a backward baseball cap, Jocelyn Guest, 34, alternated between a hook and a short skinny knife, frenching a cavernous rack of lamb to expose the bones and make it “prettier,” she said.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '50', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/27/t-magazine/27tmag-chefs-slide-6289/27tmag-chefs-slide-6289-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/27/t-magazine/27tmag-chefs-slide-6289/27tmag-chefs-slide-6289-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/27/t-magazine/27tmag-chefs-slide-6289/27tmag-chefs-slide-6289-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/27/t-magazine/27tmag-chefs-slide-6289/27tmag-chefs-slide-6289-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/27/t-magazine/27tmag-chefs-slide-6289/27tmag-chefs-slide-6289-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/27/t-magazine/27tmag-chefs-slide-6289/27tmag-chefs-slide-6289-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/27/t-magazine/27tmag-chefs-slide-6289/27tmag-chefs-slide-6289-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Female Couples Remaking the Restaurant Industry', 'kicker': 'Food Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': ' A Women’s Place…', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chefs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'I Sodi (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Via Carota (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'White Gold Butchers (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nakamura, Erika', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sodi, Rita', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Jody (1963- )', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-16T14:41:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ligaya Mishan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ligaya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mishan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f8b17b5-b59a-5d33-8111-b90390131e4b', 'word_count': 1753, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f8b17b5-b59a-5d33-8111-b90390131e4b'}, {'abstract': 'The owners of the Roman design boutique Chez Dédé create a private space where creativity can run wild.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/16/t-magazine/design/chez-dede-boutique-atelier.html', 'snippet': 'The owners of the Roman design boutique Chez Dédé create a private space where creativity can run wild.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rome is a city of pockets and alcoves. Strolling its streets, you catch glimpses of intimate spaces that exist just beyond the public facades: wisteria-draped courtyards, ivy-shrouded archways, begonias spilling from terraces. These hints of private realms beckon most alluringly from the Tiber River-adjacent Regola neighborhood, known since the Renaissance as the center for mercantile activities from plate-making to leather-stitching. It’s here, in a space in the historic Palazzo Capponi Antonelli, a 16th-century building with a pebbled cortile and a stone fountain, that the boutique Chez Dédé sells the best of contemporary Italian artisanry. In the ground-floor boutique, whose walls are hung with posters drawn by co-owner Andrea Ferolla, a 56-year-old fashion illustrator and creative director, items are arranged in inviting tableaus — a retail version of the ideal Roman home. The brand’s own patterned canvas carryalls sit atop velvet-upholstered couches, and the living room’s lampshades are sewn from vintage Arjumand’s World wallpaper; the vanity’s shelves are lined with Linda Rodin’s perfume; and beyond that, there is a closet dedicated to robes, dresses and coats by the Italian line Giuliva Heritage Collection. “I wanted to show how objects could inform each other,” says co-owner Daria Reina, a 48-year-old photographer and creative director who, with Ferolla, opened the shop three years ago. (Like many respectable creative duos, the two had a scandalous affair before becoming a couple 16 years ago, back when Reina was freelancing at an agency where Ferolla was a creative director.)', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '70', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/26/t-magazine/26tmag-chezdede-slide-79U5/26tmag-chezdede-slide-79U5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/26/t-magazine/26tmag-chezdede-slide-79U5/26tmag-chezdede-slide-79U5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/26/t-magazine/26tmag-chezdede-slide-79U5/26tmag-chezdede-slide-79U5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/26/t-magazine/26tmag-chezdede-slide-79U5/26tmag-chezdede-slide-79U5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/26/t-magazine/26tmag-chezdede-slide-79U5/26tmag-chezdede-slide-79U5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/26/t-magazine/26tmag-chezdede-slide-79U5/26tmag-chezdede-slide-79U5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/26/t-magazine/26tmag-chezdede-slide-79U5/26tmag-chezdede-slide-79U5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Secret Atelier Behind a Roman Boutique', 'kicker': 'In Studio', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Back of the House', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rome (Italy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-16T14:45:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Design & Interiors', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chiara Barzini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chiara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barzini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/573f04da-ae70-5224-87ca-1e1d7b2e3f8b', 'word_count': 879, 'uri': 'nyt://article/573f04da-ae70-5224-87ca-1e1d7b2e3f8b'}, {'abstract': 'In the first few months of Gov. Philip D. Murphy’s tenure, New Jersey has taken a decidedly liberal turn, with new laws and executive orders reading like a progressive wish list.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/16/nyregion/new-jersey-emerges-as-a-liberal-bulwark-under-murphy.html', 'snippet': 'In the first few months of Gov. Philip D. Murphy’s tenure, New Jersey has taken a decidedly liberal turn, with new laws and executive orders reading like a progressive wish list.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A recently adopted equal pay law has put New Jersey at the forefront of national efforts to narrow the gender wage gap. The state’s new automatic voter registration law ranks among the most sweeping in the country, while its funding of Planned Parenthood, package of gun control laws, renewable energy legislation and a measure to provide state financial aid to immigrants who came to the United States as children are all part of the progressive playbook.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/17/nyregion/17murphy1/merlin_137358756_48c0e795-4443-487d-ba22-6a607a72a438-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/17/nyregion/17murphy1/merlin_137358756_48c0e795-4443-487d-ba22-6a607a72a438-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/17/nyregion/17murphy1/merlin_137358756_48c0e795-4443-487d-ba22-6a607a72a438-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/17/nyregion/17murphy1/merlin_137358756_48c0e795-4443-487d-ba22-6a607a72a438-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/17/nyregion/17murphy1/17murphy1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/17/nyregion/17murphy1/17murphy1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/17/nyregion/17murphy1/17murphy1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Jersey Emerges as a Liberal Bulwark Under Murphy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Governor Tilts New Jersey Hard to the Left', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Philip D (1957- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Governors (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-16T14:52:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Corasaniti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corasaniti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e577635a-c623-588f-af4a-7c9e4d86ea5f', 'word_count': 1592, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e577635a-c623-588f-af4a-7c9e4d86ea5f'}, {'abstract': 'From good-looking lawn chairs to a lamp that resembles a ravioli, these new makers are producing pieces worth remembering. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/16/t-magazine/design/new-furniture-designers.html', 'snippet': 'From good-looking lawn chairs to a lamp that resembles a ravioli, these new makers are producing pieces worth remembering. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like any good design project, Offsite, the nomadic design fair organized by Sight Unseen founders Jill Singer and Monica Khemsurov, has gone through lots of iterations. “It was a hodgepodge when it first started,” says Singer of the showcase’s 2014 launch. Five years in, she and Khemsurov, who is a T Magazine contributor, have honed their curatorial vision: now, it is a tightly edited, weekend-long destination where avant-garde and independent design is both on display and in development. This year, Sight Unseen has tapped outlets like Opening Ceremony, 3.1 Phillip Lim and Creatures of Comfort to partner with designers on a handful of satellite venues around New York which will complement a central location at 201 Mulberry. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/15/t-magazine/15tmag-sight-unseen-slide-BDKH/15tmag-sight-unseen-slide-BDKH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/15/t-magazine/15tmag-sight-unseen-slide-BDKH/15tmag-sight-unseen-slide-BDKH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/15/t-magazine/15tmag-sight-unseen-slide-BDKH/15tmag-sight-unseen-slide-BDKH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/15/t-magazine/15tmag-sight-unseen-slide-BDKH/15tmag-sight-unseen-slide-BDKH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/15/t-magazine/15tmag-sight-unseen-slide-BDKH/15tmag-sight-unseen-slide-BDKH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/15/t-magazine/15tmag-sight-unseen-slide-BDKH/15tmag-sight-unseen-slide-BDKH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/15/t-magazine/15tmag-sight-unseen-slide-BDKH/15tmag-sight-unseen-slide-BDKH-thumbLarg