ed', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/449e09e1-1919-5724-a316-d7cf7c272a55', 'word_count': 926, 'uri': 'nyt://article/449e09e1-1919-5724-a316-d7cf7c272a55'}, {'abstract': 'A state investigation found “substantial evidence” of discrimination in North Bend, a conservative area on Oregon’s southern coast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/16/us/oregon-school-lgbt-students-bible.html', 'snippet': 'A state investigation found “substantial evidence” of discrimination in North Bend, a conservative area on Oregon’s southern coast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the hallways of a rural Oregon high school, gay and lesbian students were taunted with homophobic slurs. In the cafeteria, students pelted a transgender student with food. And when gay and lesbian students got into trouble, the school’s principal assigned a specific punishment just for them: readings from the Bible.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/17/us/17xp-oregon-print/17xp-oregon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/17/us/17xp-oregon-print/17xp-oregon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/17/us/17xp-oregon-print/17xp-oregon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/17/us/17xp-oregon-print/17xp-oregon-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name