raded Favors for Luxury Gifts, Prosecutors Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Loans for Gifts and Jobs: Long Island Prosecutors Lay Out Bribery Scheme', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Venditto, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mangano, Edward P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nassau County (NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-17T00:52:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7239b8a0-9908-5e91-b837-345efc3d8819', 'word_count': 1022, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7239b8a0-9908-5e91-b837-345efc3d8819'}, {'abstract': 'Four screen goddesses — Jane Fonda, Diane Keaton, Mary Steenburgen and Candice Bergen — play characters searching for their inner goddesses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/16/movies/book-club-review-jane-fonda-diane-keaton.html', 'snippet': 'Four screen goddesses — Jane Fonda, Diane Keaton, Mary Steenburgen and Candice Bergen — play characters searching for their inner goddesses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The four members in the titular book club of “Book Club” are four women who have been meeting once a month to drink wine and talk about a book. They started in the ’70s with Erica Jong’s “Fear of Flying” and have just turned their attention to E.L. James’s “Fifty Shades of Grey.” There’s a lot of literary and social history in the span between those two best sellers, which take their heroines from “zipless” adu