 film from Matthew Porterfield, a just-out-of-prison young man contends with bad luck and his own unwise impulses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a desultory existence for Keith (the appealing McCaul Lombardi), a young man living with his dad in the Baltimore neighborhood that gives this movie its title. He wears a bracelet on his ankle that monitors him; he’s out of prison after doing time for an unspecified crime and still under house arrest. He can’t get permission to travel out of state for a family function.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/18/arts/18sollers1/merlin_137865300_1306bb8c-5577-4599-b1cb-ca29800b6a56-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 324, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/18/arts/18sollers1/merlin_137865300_1306bb8c-5577-4599-b1cb-ca29800b6a56-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 324}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/18/arts/18sollers1/merlin_137865300_1306bb8c-5577-4599-b1cb-ca29800b6a56-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 554, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/18/arts/18sollers1/merlin_137865300_1306bb8c-5577-4599-b1cb-ca29800b6a56-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1038, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/18/arts/18sollers1/sollers1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/18/arts/18sollers1/sollers1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}},