w', '_id': 'nyt://article/65fc600b-1e88-5a1c-8e7b-a650646f43c5', 'word_count': 1039, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65fc600b-1e88-5a1c-8e7b-a650646f43c5'}, {'abstract': 'Smart signings, massive crowds and a stealthy bus ride before home games have helped an M.L.S. team foster an immediate connection with its fans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/17/sports/soccer/atlanta-united-mls.html', 'snippet': 'Smart signings, massive crowds and a stealthy bus ride before home games have helped an M.L.S. team foster an immediate connection with its fans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — Jay Riddle moved to this city of transplants 14 years ago, and for much of that time, his life revolved around his job in the aerospace industry. His main sports fix was watching Arsenal matches on television each weekend. He knew little of Major League Soccer.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/20/sports/20atlantaunited-pic-01/merlin_136791933_562282c6-04cc-470b-9115-b657c4b8ccd0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/20/sports/20atlantaunited-pic-01/merlin_136791933_562282c6-04cc-470b-9115-b657c4b8ccd0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/20/sports/20atlantaunited-pic-01/merlin_136791933_562282c6-04cc-470b-9115-b657c4b8ccd0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/20/sports/20atlantaunited-pic-01/merlin_136791933_562282c6-04cc-470b-9115-b657c4b8ccd0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/20/sports/20atlantaunited-pic-01/20atlantaunited-pic-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/20/sports/20atlantaunited-pic-01/20atlantaunited-pic-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/20/sports/20atlantaunited-pic-01/20atlantaunited-pic-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Atlanta, United by Soccer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Football Country Goes Crazy For a Soccer Team', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlanta United FC (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Soccer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blank, Arthur M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-17T15:10:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cc2a0e4-7f9d-5595-8c00-1db624a42b2c', 'word_count': 1692, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cc2a0e4-7f9d-5595-8c00-1db624a42b2c'}, {'abstract': 'Activities to both teach with and teach about the genre, with help from dozens of Times comics, articles, essays and videos.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/17/learning/lesson-plans/from-superheroes-to-syrian-refugees-teaching-comics-and-graphic-novels-with-resources-from-the-new-york-times.html', 'snippet': 'Activities to both teach with and teach about the genre, with help from dozens of Times comics, articles, essays and videos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On this site, we’re all about visual literacy, and some of our most popular features — from our Monday What’s Going On in This Picture? photojournalism exercise to our Friday Film Club to our daily Picture Prompts — were invented to use great New York Times multimedia storytelling to help students better understand the news, our culture and how current events can relate to their lives.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/02/magazine/new-york-stories-introduction-1496394862777-LN/new-york-stories-introduction-1496394862777-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 572, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/06/02/magazine/new-york-stories-introduction-1496394862777-LN/new-york-stories-introduction-1496394862777-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 572}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/02/magazine/new-york-stories-introduction-1496394862777-LN/new-york-stories-introduction-1496394862777-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 975, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/02/magazine/new-york-stories-introduction-1496394862777-LN/new-york-stories-introduction-1496394862777-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1905, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/02/maga