c-books-teaching.html', 'snippet': 'The reporter who covers the comic-book industry for The Times describes how a lifetime love of comics has taught him about science, history, and himself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As part of the Learning Network’s collection about teaching with comics and graphic novels, we asked George Gene Gustines, The Times’s reporter on the comic-book industry, to tell us about his job. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/15/learning/TeenTitansLN/TeenTitansLN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 575, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/15/learning/TeenTitansLN/TeenTitansLN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 575, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/15/learning/TeenTitansLN/TeenTitansLN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/15/learning/TeenTitansLN/TeenTitansLN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/15/learning/TeenTitansLN/TeenTitansLN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Comic Books Turned a Fan into a Professional, and Educated Him Along the Way', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2018-05-17T15:11:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/068d93c1-0e8e-58a1-81cf-fdee5b361068', 'word_count': 1985, 'uri': 'nyt://article/068d93c1-0e8e-58a1-81cf-fdee5b361068'}, {'abstract': 'The attorney general has taken personal charge of a case that could mean the end of asylum status for domestic violence victims in the U.S.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/17/opinion/jeff-sessions-asylum-domestic-violence.html', 'snippet': 'The attorney general has taken personal charge of a case that could mean the end of asylum status for domestic violence victims in the U.S.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In recent years, the United States has been something of a beacon of hope for women fleeing violence and persecution in their home countries. In 2014, in a giant step forward, immigration courts explicitly determined that a person fleeing severe domestic violence may be granted asylum here if the violence rises to the level of persecution, if the government in the victim’s home country cannot or will not punish her abuser and if various other criteria are met. It’s a high bar but one that, sadly, women from many countries can clear. Now their last chance at protection may be under threat.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/17/opinion/17fonda-illo/17fonda-illo-articleLarge-v6.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/17/opinion/17fonda-illo/17fonda-illo-articleLarge-v6.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/17/opinion/17fonda-illo/17fonda-illo-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/17/opinion/17fonda-illo/17fonda-illo-superJumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/17/opinion/17fonda-illo/17fonda-illo-thumbStandard-v6.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/17/opinion/17fonda-illo/17fonda-illo-thumbStandard-v6.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/17/opinion/17fonda-illo/17fonda-illo-thumbLarge-v6.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Her Husband Beat Her and Raped Her. Jeff Sessions Might Deport Her.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beaten, Raped and Put in Limbo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asylum, Right of', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Domestic Violence', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sessions, Jefferson B III', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-17T15:11:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Fonda and Karen Musalo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fonda', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Musalo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c3fc061-7089-5073-84ff-f4a5eb538021', 'word_count': 855, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c3fc061-7089-5073-84ff-f4a5eb538021'}, {'abstract': 'Do you think more comics and graphic novels should be taught in schools? Which ones would you recommend?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/17/learning/what-have-you-learned-from-comics.html', 'snippet': 'Do you think more comics and graphic novels should be taught in schools? Which ones would you recommend?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Do you read comics and graphic novels? If so, what do you enjoy about them? Which are your favorites? What are you reading now?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/23/arts/23comics-1-LN/23comics-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 928, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/09/23/arts/23comics-1-LN/23comics-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 928}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/23/arts/23comics-1-LN/23comics-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 663, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/23/arts/23comics-1-LN/23comics-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1325, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/23/arts/23comics-1-LN/23comics-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/09/23/arts/23comics-1-LN/23comics-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/23/arts/23comics-1-LN/23comics-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Have You Learned from Comics?', 'kicker': 'Student Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2018-05-17T15:11:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By Natalie Proulx', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Natalie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Proulx', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1490291-50ba-5511-89be-4ce3f647c3a0', 'word_count': 639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1490291-50ba-5511-89be-4ce3f647c3a0'}, {'abstract': 'The jewelry designer first went to Japan as a teenager and became enamored; now, Eastern design has suffused her home in Saint-Germain-des-Prés, Paris.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/17/t-magazine/fashion/gaia-repossi-japanese-bud-vases.html', 'snippet': 'The jewelry designer first went to Japan as a teenager and became enamored; now, Eastern design has suffused her home in Saint-Germain-des-Prés, Paris.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Parisian jewelry designer Gaia Repossi made her first trip to Japan as a teenager 14 years ago — and she’s returned virtually every year since. “I came home with an extra suitcase full of crafts and the most amazing drawing materials,” she says. “Now I only work with Japanese stencils, technical drawing pens, paper and notebooks.” Repossi’s love for the powerful simplicity of Japanese design has influenced the spare, architectural fine jewelry she creates for her family’s namesake house, where she serves as creative director; she often revisits the temples of Kyoto and the island of Naoshima, where architect Tadao Ando’s structures abound, for inspiration. Eastern design has suffused her home in Saint-Germain-des-Prés, Paris, too — including an extensive collection of bud vases made by Japanese potters and Western artisans, who, like herself, are enamored of those traditions. “It’s something about the shapes and the way they take on color. It’s an aesthetic that’s timeless, yet so advanced,” says Repossi. “They remind me of little jewelry pieces.”', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '150', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/26/t-magazine/26tmag-ofakind-slide-NM6N/26tmag-ofakind-slide-NM6N-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/26/t-magazine/26tmag-ofakind-slide-NM6N/26tmag-ofakind-slide-NM6N-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/26/t-magazine/26tmag-ofakind-slide-NM6N/26tmag-ofakind-slide-NM6N-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/26/t-magazine/26tmag-ofakind-slide-NM6N/26tmag-ofakind-slide-NM6N-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1067, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/26/t-magazine/26tmag-ofakind-slide-NM6N/26tmag-ofakind-slide-NM6N-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/26/t-magazine/26tmag-ofak