le comedian to a cultural provocateur and authority on blackness. We like Glover’s brain and the music and TV he is making, but we also wonder about the speed with which he’s been anointed a “genius.” Who gets left out when we apply that label so liberally to men? What do women have to do to be considered geniuses? More specifically, why aren’t we using that term for black women? And is there such a thing as black male privilege?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/briefing/17still-processing/09Eveningbriefing-slide-FX1M-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/09/briefing/17still-processing/09Eveningbriefing-slide-FX1M-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/briefing/17still-processing/09Eveningbriefing-slide-FX1M-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/briefing/17still-processing/09Eveningbriefing-slide-FX1M-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/09/briefing/17still-processing/09Eveningbriefing-slide-FX1M-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/09/briefing/17still-processing/09Eveningbriefing-slide-FX1M-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/0