}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Democratic Women Surge, Ranks of Republican Women May Shrink', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Democratic Surge  May Thin G.O.P. Ranks Of Women in Capitol', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Emily's List", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Republican Congressional Committee', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2018)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-17T18:45:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheryl Gay Stolberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheryl', 'middlename': 'Gay', 'lastname': 'Stolberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/520c02c0-f8aa-5a88-bbb1-02b56fa598bb', 'word_count': 1338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/520c02c0-f8aa-5a88-bbb1-02b56fa598bb'}, {'abstract': "Where to stay, eat, and explore on the remote subtropical island off Japan's southern coast.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/17/t-magazine/travel/yakushima-japan-guide.html', 'snippet': "Where to stay, eat, and explore on the remote subtropical island off Japan's southern coast.", 'lead_paragraph': 'The small, remote island of Yakushima, which lies off the southern coast of the southernmost of Japan’s four major islands, Kyushu, is shaped something like the Hawaiian isle of Kauai. And just as on that other circular bit of rock over 4,000 miles away across the North Pacific, visitors arrive here seeking respite in subtropical rain forests and mountains — and along the miles of untouched coastline, where endangered loggerhead and green turtles nest. But what’s startling about Yakushima is the absence of crowds and over-commercialization, even with its easy proximity to Osaka, an hour-and-a-half-long flight away. (There are also two ports on the island — in Miyanoura and Anbo — from where multiple daily ferry services connect to the town of Kagoshima on Kyushu.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/17/t-magazine/travel/yakushima-slide-YDS9/yakushima-slide-YDS9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/17/t-magazine/travel/yakushima-slide-YDS9/yakushima-slide-YDS9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/17/t-magazine/travel/yakushima-slide-YDS9/yakushima-slide-YDS9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/17/t-magazine/travel/yakushima-slide-YDS9/yakushima-slide-YDS9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/17/t-magazine/travel/yakushima-slide-YDS9/yakushima-slide-YDS9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/17/t-magazine/travel/yakushima-slide-YDS9/yakushima-slide-YDS9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/17/t-magazine/travel/yakushima-slide-YDS9/yakushima-slide-YDS9-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Guide to the Otherworldly Island of Yakushima', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japanese Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-17T18:48:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Wogan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wogan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1ed6831-8dac-54ba-b23a-7f39308fdc1f', 'word_count': 1097, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1ed6831-8dac-54ba-b23a-7f39308fdc1f'}, {'abstract': 'Finding echoes of Japan’s ancient past, and of the woodlands of Hayao Miyazaki’s animated masterpiece “Princess Mononoke,” deep among the trees of Yakushima island.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/17/t-magazine/yakushima-japan-hayao-miyazaki-princess-mononoke.html', 'snippet': 'Finding echoes of Japan’s ancient past, and of the woodlands of Hayao Miyazaki’s animated masterpiece “Princess Mononoke,” deep among the trees of Yakushima island.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN ORDER TO see one of the oldest living trees on earth in one of the oldest evergreen forests in the world, you must first fly two hours from Tokyo to the town of Kagoshima on Kyushu, which is the southern- and westernmost of Japan’s four major islands. From there, you board a little twin-propeller plane for another short flight south to Yakushima, which appears on maps as a near-perfect circle, the last piece of significant landmass before the Okinawa archipelago, another hour’s flight south.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/26/t-magazine/26tmag-yakushima-slide-6F6U/26tmag-yakushima-slide-6F6U-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 249, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/26/t-magazine/26tmag-yakushima-slide-6F6U/26tmag-yakushima-slide-6F6U-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 249}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/26/t-magazine/26tmag-yakushima-slide-6F6U/26tmag-yakushima-slide-6F6U-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 425, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/26/t-magazine/26tmag-yakushima-slide-6F6U/26tmag-yakushima-slide-6F6U-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 850, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/26/t-magazine/26tmag-yakushima-slide-6F6U/26tmag-yakushima-slide-6F6U-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/26/t-magazine/26tmag-yakushima-slide-6F6U/26tmag-yakushima-slide-6F6U-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/26/t-magazine/26tmag-yakushima-slide-6F6U/26tmag-yakushima-slide-6F6U-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'widt