 present. This week: J.D. Scott reviews “The Old Boys.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cynthia Ozick reviews “Last Stories,” William Trevor’s final collection of stories, for this week’s cover. In 1964, J.D. Scott reviewed the Irish author’s debut novel, “The Old Boys,” for the Book Review. Below is an excerpt.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Notes From the Book Review Archives', 'kicker': 'Our Back Pages', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-18T15:09:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9eac7f8-f645-588c-a66f-1cc77ecf526b', 'word_count': 380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9eac7f8-f645-588c-a66f-1cc77ecf526b'}, {'abstract': 'Whether “Cheers” is an old favorite or you still need an introduction, these nine standout episodes provide a great time-lapse portrait of the show.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/18/watching/cheers-best-episodes.html', 'snippet': 'Whether “Cheers” is an old favorite or you still need an introduction, these nine standout episodes provide a great time-lapse portrait of the show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Watching is The New York Times’s TV and film recommendation website. Sign up for our thrice-weekly newsletter here.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/watching/21cheers-best/18cheers-best-slide-0E1C-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/21/watching/21chee