ew-york-landlord-tenant-rights.html', 'snippet': 'The city’s housing system can be complicated to navigate. Here’s a quick primer on what your rights are and how to exercise them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York’s roughly one million rent-regulated apartments make up the largest portion of affordable housing in the city. Officially, there are mechanisms in place not only to govern the amount of rent charged for these units but also, crucially, to protect the rights of the people who live in them. In practice, though, the burden largely falls on tenants to be proactive in holding their landlords to account.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/22/nyregion/22Housing-know1/merlin_138308601_7e723471-0113-4494-b301-062c5300d14a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/22/nyregion/22Housing-know1/merlin_138308601_7e723471-0113-4494-b301-062c5300d14a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/22/nyregion/22Housing-know1/merlin_138308601_7e723471-0113-4494-b301-062c5300d14a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/22/nyregion/22Housing-know1/merlin_138308601_7e723471-0113-4494-b301-062c5300d14a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/22/nyregion/22Housing-know1/22Housing-know1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 