g', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Right Way to Fix the Prisons', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Right Way to Fix the Prisons', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mandatory Sentencing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sessions, Jefferson B III', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-20T22:57:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/fdebce26-b3ba-5d86-8157-2b910a3b5c2f', 'word_count': 930, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fdebce26-b3ba-5d86-8157-2b910a3b5c2f'}, {'abstract': 'Employers are complaining about labor shortages. Why won’t they raise wages?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/20/opinion/monopsony-rigidity-and-the-wage-puzzle-wonkish.html', 'snippet': 'Employers are complaining about labor shortages. Why won’t they raise wages?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Once a year my academic base, CUNY’s Stone Center on Socio-Economic Inequality, holds a workshop featuring cutting-edge research on inequality. At this point in my life, I can’t claim to be doing cutting-edge research (hey, even Paul Samuelson was writing mostly survey papers and history of thought by the time he was in his 60s); but I’m still asked to give a talk on research issues that I find interesting, hopefully with some relationship to the general theme of the workshop. One virtue of this grand-old-man role, by the way, is that it forces me to tear myself away for a little while from the awful political headlines.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/20/opinion/20krugman/merlin_47698189_5ab49382-6270-4b3f-a6ca-3ffde9e85164-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 454, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/20/opinion/20krugman/merlin_47698189_5ab49382-6270-4b3f-a6ca-3ffde9e85164-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 454}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/20/opinion/20krugman/merlin_47698189_5ab49382-6270-4b3f-a6ca-3ffde9e85164-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 774, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/20/opinion/20krugman/merlin_47698189_5ab49382-6270-4b3f-a6ca-3ffde9e85164-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1548, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/20/opinion/20krugman/merlin_47698189_5ab49382-6270-4b3f-a6ca-3ffde9e85164-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/20/opinion/20krugman/merlin_47698189_5ab49382-6270-4b3f-a6ca-3ffde9e85164-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None,