es.com/2018/05/21/opinion/venzuela-maduro-election.html', 'snippet': 'I wasn’t sure, so I went looking for a true believer, of any kind, at the polling stations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CIUDAD GUAYANA, Venezuela — Sunday, 5 a.m. The military has already closed all the streets near voting centers, including mine. This is typical on election day. Also typical on election day is the sound of the military trumpet, the toque de diana, at the break of dawn. I’m looking out the balcony window of my apartment thinking it’ll ring out any second now.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/opinion/21hernandez/21hernandez-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/21/opinion/21hernandez/21hernandez-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/opinion/21hernandez/21hernandez-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/opinion/21hernandez/21hernandez-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/opinion/21hernandez/21hernandez-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/21/opinion/21hernandez/21hernandez-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/opinion/21hernandez/21hernandez-thu