.html', 'snippet': 'The genome obviously varies from person to person. But it can also vary from cell to cell, even within the same individual. The implications of “mosaicism” are enormous.', 'lead_paragraph': 'James Priest couldn’t make sense of it. He was examining the DNA of a desperately ill baby, searching for a genetic mutation that threatened to stop her heart. But the results looked as if they had come from two different infants.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/22/science/22MOSAICISM/merlin_138329916_800bc565-7a98-421a-a4ab-795a32b29624-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 705, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/22/science/22MOSAICISM/merlin_138329916_800bc565-7a98-421a-a4ab-795a32b29624-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 705}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/22/science/22MOSAICISM/merlin_138329916_800bc565-7a98-421a-a4ab-795a32b29624-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 873, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/22/science/22MOSAICISM/merlin_138329916_800bc565-7a98-421a-a4ab-795a32b29624-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 1022, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/22/science/22MOSAICISM/22MOSAICISM-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/22/science/22MOSAICISM/22MOSAICISM-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/22/science/22MOSAICISM/22MOSAICISM-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Every Cell in Your Body Has the Same DNA. Except It Doesn’t.', 'kicker': 'Matter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Hidden Identity Crisis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chromosomes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biology and Biochemistry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Darwin, Charles Robert', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-21T19:38:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Zimmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zimmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e47bd91-d752-5399-9eaf-87138031b363', 'word_count': 2206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e47bd91-d752-5399-9eaf-87138031b363'}, {'abstract': 'A new flavor from Josephine’s Feast combines lush berries with pink Champagne.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/21/dining/strawberry-preserves-pink-champagne.html', 'snippet': 'A new flavor from Josephine’s Feast combines lush berries with pink Champagne.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Josephine’s Feast, a Brooklyn producer of preserves and condiments made mostly from local ingredients (even foraged beach plums), has welcomed summer with a fragrant new flavor, strawberries and pink Champagne. It has been recognized as a notable new product by the Specialty Food Association, the trade group that runs the Fancy Food Show, which will take place in New York next month. Thick, with plump berries that have a winey complexity, the preserves deserve freshly baked muffins or scones. You could even drop a dollop or two into a glass of bubbly: Strawberries and Pink Champagne Preserves, $10 for eight ounces, josephinesfeast.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/23/dining/23burnerpreserves/merlin_138149661_e1146a6f-11e9-4a16-9fad-a7bcaf412a78-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/23/dining/23burnerpreserves/merlin_138149661_e1146a6f-11e9-4a16-9fad-a7bcaf412a78-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/23/dining/23burnerpreserves/merlin_138149661_e1146a6f-11e9-4a16-9fad-a7bcaf412a78-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/23/dining/23burnerpreserves/merlin_138149661_e1146a6f-11e9-4a16-9fad-a7bcaf412a78-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/23/dining/23burnerpreserves/23burnerpreserves-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/23/dining/23burnerpreserves/23burnerpreserves-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/23/dining/23burnerpreserves/23burnerpreserves-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Strawberry Preserves Worthy of a Champagne Toast', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Spread: Strawberry Preserves For Toast, and Toasting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Josephine's Feast", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jams and Jellies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Champagne (Wine)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strawberries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-21T19:44:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b47ad43-1285-5471-a0ae-28644e793018', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b47ad43-1285-5471-a0ae-28644e793018'}, {'abstract': 'Employees who are underpaid, harassed or discriminated against have been left to press their cases alone in arbitration.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/21/opinion/supreme-court-arbitration-forced.html', 'snippet': 'Employees who are underpaid, harassed or discriminated against have been left to press their cases alone in arbitration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Supreme Court has just told the nation’s workers: If you’re underpaid at work, or if you face discrimination on the job, you’re on your own.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/opinion/21gerstein/merlin_106704742_f4dc85d9-97d5-4835-bc30-ca6b0eb2c6c7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/21/opinion/21gerstein/merlin_106704742_f4dc85d9-97d5-4835-bc30-ca6b0eb2c6c7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/opinion/21gerstein/merlin_106704742_f4dc85d9-97d5-4835-bc30-ca6b0eb2c6c7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/opinion/21gerstein/merlin_106704742_f4dc85d9-97d5-4835-bc30-ca6b0eb2c6c7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/opinion/21gerstein/21gerstein-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/21/opinion/21gerstein/21gerstein-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/opinion/21gerstein/21gerstein-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Supreme Court Deals a Blow to Workers', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARBITRATION, CONCILIATION AND MEDIATION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Hazards and Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collective Bargaining', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gorsuch, Neil M', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-21T19:44:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Terri Gerstein and Sharon Block', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Terri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gerstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sharon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Block', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/72b519c5-5f96-585f-812b-135e22135848', 'word_count': 732, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72b519c5-5f96-585f-812b-135e22135848'}, {'abstract': 'Sunday’s vote giving Nicolás Maduro another term was flawed by low turnout and rampant corruption. Venezuela’s Latin neighbors must unite to isolate and force him from office.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/21/opinion/venezuela-maduro-sham-election.html', 'snippet': 'Sunday’s vote giving Nicolás Maduro another term was flawed by low turnout and rampant corruption. Venezuela’s Latin neighbors must unite to isolate and force him from office.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The issue in Venezuela is not whether Nicolás Maduro won another term fairly or not. Neither the Lima Group of Latin American countries plus Canada, nor the United States or the European Union recognized the election as legitimate. The question is how to get rid of Mr. Maduro before he completes the destruction of his country.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/opinion/21venezuelaEDT/21venezuelaEDT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/21/opinion/21venezuelaEDT/21venezuelaEDT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/opinion/21venezuelaEDT/21venezuelaEDT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/opinion/21venezuelaEDT/21venezuelaEDT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1355, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/opinion/21venezuelaEDT/21venezuelaEDT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/21/opinion/21venezuelaEDT/21venezuelaEDT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/opinion/21venezuelaEDT/21venezuelaEDT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Venezuela’s Sham Election', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Hugo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maduro, Nicolas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-21T19:45:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/745a2e06-780b-529a-845e-4c4ecf6db095', 'word_count': 624, 'uri': 'nyt://article/745a2e06-780b-529a-845e-4c4ecf6db095'}, {'abstract': 'A new denim item from Food52 is trendy while cutting down on waste.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/21/dining/denim-flatware-place-setting.html', 'snippet': 'A new denim item from Food52 is trendy while cutting down on waste.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m one of those annoying people who decants containers of milk or juice into pitchers and prefers cloth napkins at the table. So among the scores of clever items on the Food52 website, these denim silverware wraps caught my eye. They neatly hold a place setting and can also be used as napkins or place mats at the picnic table or even on a lap. They are an investment, and though they have to be laundered after use, the plus side is that they will not add to the trash: Denim flatware place setting, $42 for two, $76 for four, food52.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/23/dining/23burnercarry/merlin_137608320_53c80d39-af0f-4fef-953e-7cf7bf45e955-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/23/dining/23burnercarry/merlin_137608320_53c80d39-af0f-4fef-953e-7cf7bf45