s', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5baa505-c3b7-5dc0-9c95-d86c8b410d0e', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5baa505-c3b7-5dc0-9c95-d86c8b410d0e'}, {'abstract': 'Here’s what you need to know to start your day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/21/briefing/china-north-korea-pope-francis.html', 'snippet': 'Here’s what you need to know to start your day.', 'lead_paragraph': '(Want to get this briefing by email? Here’s the sign-up.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/briefing/052218Asia-briefing-promo/052218Asia-briefing-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/21/briefing/052218Asia-briefing-promo/052218Asia-briefing-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/briefing/052218Asia-briefing-promo/052218Asia-briefing-promo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 188, 'width': 624, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/briefing/052218Asia-briefing-promo/052218Asia-briefing-promo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 188, 'width': 624, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/briefing/052218Asia-briefing-promo/052218Asia-briefing-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/21/briefing/052218Asia-briefing-promo/052218Asia-briefing-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/briefing/052218Asia-briefing-promo/052218Asia-briefing-promo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'China, North Korea, Pope Francis: Your Tuesday Briefing', 'kicker': 'Asia and Australia Edition', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2018-05-21T19:53:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NYTNow', 'section_name': 'Briefing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Levin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Levin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b03f6b6-1aed-5388-a994-59756133d509', 'word_count': 1358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b03f6b6-1aed-5388-a994-59756133d509'}, {'abstract': '“Lemonade With Zest” traces a summertime treat to ancient Egypt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/21/dining/lemonade-with-zest-book-april-white.html', 'snippet': '“Lemonade With Zest” traces a summertime treat to ancient Egypt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You may think making lemonade is easy. Not when you’re reading about an 11th-century Egyptian mixture of lemon juice and sugar called qatarmizat, supposedly a proto-lemonade, in “Lemonade With Zest.” I would have thought the Romans knew about it, but it seems that the lemon was not known in those days. This slender volume offers basic ingredients and recipes for lemonades, most of which are sweetened, wisely, with simple syrups. You’ll find slushy, frozen lemonades, some made with melon, sumac, cardamom, coffee and mint, and recipes for sherbets, sorbets, granitas and shrubs, with suggestions for cocktails along the way: “Lemonade With Zest: 40 Thirst-Quenching Recipes” by April White (Chronicle Books, $16.95)', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/23/dining/23burnerlemonade/-23burnerlemonade-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 804, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/23/dining/23burnerlemonade/-23burnerlemonade-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 804}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/23/dining/23burnerlemonade/-23burnerlemonade-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 765, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/23/dining/23burnerlemonade/-23burnerlemonade-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1529, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/23/dining/23burnerlemonade/23burnerlemonade-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/23/dining/23burnerlemonade/23burnerlemonade-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/23/dining/23burnerlemonade/23burnerlemonade-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Tome to Turn to When Life Gives You Lemons', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Refresh: Squeezing History Out of Lemonade', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lemons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-21T19:56:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/362f4d8c-87e6-5318-aa95-59482fa63bda', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/362f4d8c-87e6-5318-aa95-59482fa63bda'}, {'abstract': 'Our/Vodka’s latest urban distillery opens this week in Chelsea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/21/dining/vodka-our-new-york-distillery.html', 'snippet': 'Our/Vodka’s latest urban distillery opens this week in Chelsea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though distilleries in Brooklyn and on Long Island have been making local spirits for some time, Our/New York will be the first distillery in Manhattan since Prohibition when it opens to the public on Friday. The copper pot still, or alembic, sits behind the spacious bar like a shiny visitor from outer space. The project is part of Our/Vodka, which makes city-specific spirits (Amsterdam, Berlin, Detroit, London and Los Angeles are the others). All are small-batch distilleries that depend mostly on the local water for their whisper of differences. The New York vodka, 80-proof and served in drinks or sold by the bottle, was a tad fruity; the Los Angeles sample finished sweetly. A 100-proof version with a slightly richer mouthfeel is available only at the distillery. The bar also serves basic snacks: Our/New York, 80-proof, $22.99 for 375 milliliters, 151 West 26th Street (Seventh Avenue), 646-753-5556, ourvodka.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/23/dining/23burnervodka/23burnervodka-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'widt