person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/c621dac7-2a1c-5f96-82dc-a29ab5c9e3e8', 'word_count': 1142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c621dac7-2a1c-5f96-82dc-a29ab5c9e3e8'}, {'abstract': 'On the 20th anniversary of her project “Girl Pictures,” the photographer Justine Kurland looks back at her now-iconic images.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2018/05/21/t-magazine/justine-kurlands-timeless-photographs-of-runaway-girls.html', 'snippet': 'On the 20th anniversary of her project “Girl Pictures,” the photographer Justine Kurland looks back at her now-iconic images.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the 20th anniversary of her project “Girl Pictures,” the photographer Justine Kurland looks back at her now-iconic images.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/t-magazine/21tmag-kurland-slide-3YWK/21tmag-kurland-slide-3YWK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 470, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/21/t-magazine/21tmag-kurland-slide-3YWK/21tmag-kurland-slide-3YWK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 470}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/t-magazine/21tmag-kurland-slide-3YWK/21tmag-kurland-slide-3YWK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 802, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/t-magazine/21tmag-kurland-slide-3YWK/21tmag-kurland-slide-3YWK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1604, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/t-magazine/21tmag-kurland-slide-3YWK/21tmag-kurland-slide-3YWK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/21/t-magazine/21tmag-kurland-slide-3YWK/21tmag-kurland-slide-3YWK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/t-magazine/21tmag-kurland-slide-3YWK/21tmag-kurland-slide-3YWK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Justine Kurland’s Timeless Photographs of Runaway Girls', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2018-05-22T00:26:37+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/c65129b0-777b-55b4-a1bc-4cc8aff2c072', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/c65129b0-777b-55b4-a1bc-4cc8aff2c072'}, {'abstract': 'Justine Kurland’s images of adolescence are just as poignant 20 years after her project debuted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/21/t-magazine/justine-kurland-girl-pictures.html', 'snippet': 'Justine Kurland’s images of adolescence are just as poignant 20 years after her project debuted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The photographer Justine Kurland didn’t learn how to drive until she was 27, a year before she set off on a two-decade-long road trip. At the time, she was an M.F.A. candidate at Yale working on her now-iconic series “Girl Pictures” (1997-2002), staged portraits of adolescent girls cast as runaways wandering beneath highway overpasses and mucking around in roadside drainage ditches. At first she stayed close to home, shooting in and around New Haven, Conn., but eventually she began traveling farther afield; she wanted her own process to reflect the stories her images told. “If the girls were running away,” she tells T, “then it made sense that I should, too.” From 1998 onward, Kurland crisscrossed the country shooting Huckleberry Finn-meets-riot grrrl vignettes — a gang of Ophelias paddling in a lake; a pair of girls carrying a slain deer through the woods; a trio scaling the burned-out shell of a car. Later, she moved on to other subjects, including hippies on communes and train-hopping drifters.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/t-magazine/21tmag-kurland-slide-ECQ7/21tmag-kurland-slide-ECQ7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 470, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/21/t-magazine/21tmag-kurland-slide-ECQ7/21tmag-kurland-slide-ECQ7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 470}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/t-magazine/21tmag-kurland-slide-ECQ7/21tmag-kurland-slide-ECQ7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 801, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/t-magazine/21tmag-kurland-slide-ECQ7/21tmag-kurland-slide-ECQ7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1603, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/t-magazine/21tmag-kurland-slide-ECQ7/21tmag-kurland-slide-ECQ7-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy