d their accessories.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/t-magazine/21tmag-clavicle-slide-RCI6/21tmag-clavicle-slide-RCI6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/21/t-magazine/21tmag-clavicle-slide-RCI6/21tmag-clavicle-slide-RCI6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/t-magazine/21tmag-clavicle-slide-RCI6/21tmag-clavicle-slide-RCI6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/t-magazine/21tmag-clavicle-slide-RCI6/21tmag-clavicle-slide-RCI6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/t-magazine/21tmag-clavicle-slide-RCI6/21tmag-clavicle-slide-RCI6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/21/t-magazine/21tmag-clavicle-slide-RCI6/21tmag-clavicle-slide-RCI6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/t-magazine/21tmag-clavicle-slide-RCI6/21tmag-clavicle-slide-RCI6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Clavicle Studies From the Royal Wedding', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2018-05-22T00:32:33+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/e0a482fd-1d13-5c13-9076-bf2234937420', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/e0a482fd-1d13-5c13-9076-bf2234937420'}, {'abstract': 'The photographer Alexander Coggin zoomed in on the clavicles of many of the revelers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/21/t-magazine/royal-wedding-fans-crowd-photos.html', 'snippet': 'The photographer Alexander Coggin zoomed in on the clavicles of many of the revelers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The royal wedding of Prince Harry and Meghan Markle, now the Duke and Duchess of Sussex, featured Amal Clooney in mustard yellow, Oprah in a regal fascinator — but for many of the fans and royal watchers who weren’t formally invited, the nuptials presented an opportunity to dress up, too. The American photographer Alexander Coggin went out to capture the scene on the packed streets of Windsor — but instead of taking portraits of the revelers, he zoomed in for close-ups of their collarbones. The results are the latest images in his “Clavicle Studies” series, a project that he says gives “me authorship to focus on one specific and very telling part of the body and fashion template.” From Meghan and Harry neck scarves to lots and lots of Union Jacks, click through our slideshow to see highlights.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/24/t-magazine/21tmag-clavicle-slide-5840/21tmag-clavicle-slide-5840-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/24/t-magazine/21tmag-clavicle-slide-5840/21tmag-clavicle-slide-5840-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subty