 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27Ethicist-01/27Ethicist-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27Ethicist-01/27Ethicist-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27Ethicist-01/27Ethicist-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Should I Go to a College I’ve Been Admitted to as a Legacy?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Should I Go To a College I’ve Been Admitted to As a Legacy?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wills and Estates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-22T09:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kwame Anthony Appiah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kwame', 'middlename': 'Anthony', 'lastname': 'Appiah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28fa486f-8814-5b64-b4e9-5ae0545025ce', 'word_count': 1051, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28fa486f-8814-5b64-b4e9-5ae0545025ce'}, {'abstract': 'The “Atlanta” director on “This Is America,” surrealism and horror.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/22/magazine/hiro-murai-doesnt-want-to-get-on-a-soapbox.html', 'snippet': 'The “Atlanta” director on “This Is America,” surrealism and horror.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The music video you directed for Donald Glover/Childish Gambino’s song “This Is America” was so popular it helped propel the track to the top of the Billboard Hot 100. Were you surprised by the reaction to it? I didn’t expect it to click with people that much. But, uh, Donald knows something.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '50', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27mag-Talk3/27mag-Talk3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27mag-Talk3/27mag-Talk3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27mag-Talk3/27mag-Talk3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27mag-Talk3/27mag-Talk3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27mag-Talk3/27mag-Talk3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27mag-Talk3/27mag-Talk3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27mag-Talk3/27mag-Talk3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hiro Murai Doesn’t Want to Get on a Soapbox', 'kicker': 'Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hiro Murai Doesn’t Want to Get on a Soapbox', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FX (TV Network)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Glover, Donald', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miyazaki, Hayao', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murai, Hiro', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Atlanta (TV Program)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-22T09:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Interview by Molly Lambert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Interview', 'middlename': 'Molly', 'lastname': 'Lambert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b5aefc8-0d6f-5bc9-aaa7-12ee98d6465f', 'word_count': 661, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b5aefc8-0d6f-5bc9-aaa7-12ee98d6465f'}, {'abstract': 'Pasta tahdig combines the best of Italian and Iranian cooking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/22/magazine/pasta-tahdig-crispy-leftovers-main-course-noodles-persian-italian.html', 'snippet': 'Pasta tahdig combines the best of Italian and Iranian cooking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like all Iranian kids, I grew up feeling strongly that the best part of dinner was tahdig, the crisp, golden crust that forms at the bottom of every pot of Persian rice — and sometimes other dishes too. My mother could make it of almost anything. When she couldn’t find thin flatbreads, she used large flour tortillas — conveniently already cut into circles to line the bottom of the pot for bread tahdig. My favorite was her spaghetti tahdig. After coating pasta with tomato-rich meat sauce, my mom would drizzle the bottom of a nonstick pot with oil and put it all back in to form a dark crust of tangled noodles. Once she unmolded it at the table like a cake, my brothers and I would excitedly cut into it, verbally laying claim to our preferred pieces. I loved the brownest parts where the tomato had threatened to burn, yielding sharp, sweet bites.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27Eat1-promo/27Eat1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27Eat1-promo/27Eat1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27Eat1-promo/27Eat1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27Eat1-promo/27Eat1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27Eat1-promo/27Eat1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27Eat1-promo/27Eat1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27Eat1-promo/27Eat1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Crispy Leftovers as the Main Course', 'kicker': 'Eat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Put a Crust on It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pasta', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Noodles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-22T09:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Samin Nosrat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Samin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nosrat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/feeed33e-2cee-5bb5-8357-244e26ad44e8', 'word_count': 941, 'uri': 'nyt://article/feeed33e-2cee-5bb5-8357-244e26ad44e8'}, {'abstract': 'A selection of books published this week; plus, a peek at what our colleagues around the newsroom are reading.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/22/books/review/new-noteworthy-rumaan-alam.html', 'snippet': 'A selection of books published this week; plus, a peek at what our colleagues around the newsroom are reading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TWILIGHT OF THE GODS By Steven Hyden. (Dey Street, $25.99.) As the rock icons of the 20th century become increasingly geriatric, Hyden explores the history and significance of groups like the Rolling Stones, Fleetwood Mac and the Eagles — and how their music changed the culture. SH*TSHOW By Charlie LeDuff. (Penguin Press, $27.) LeDuff, a journalist often given the moniker “gonzo,” traveled the country seeking out real Americans, putting him on the front lines of what he calls the decline of the United States. FACTS AND FEARS By James R. Clapper with Trey Brown. (Viking, $30.) Clapper’s memoir covers his eventful years as director of national intelligence, a period that spanned the raid on Osama bin Laden, the Benghazi attack, the leaks of Edward Snowden and — most consequentially — Russia’s interference in the last presidential election. THE SUMMER I MET JACK By Michelle Gable. (St. Martin’s, $27.99.) This novel is based on the real story of Alicia Darr, a postwar refugee who worked in the Kennedy compound in Hyannis Port, Mass. From there some imagination takes over as Gable recounts this unlikely love story of a future president’s romance with the European maid. HARVEY MILK By Lillian Faderman. (Yale, $25.) The first openly gay man elected to public office in the United States, Harvey Milk was a San Francisco city supervisor until his assassination in 1978. Faderman puts Milk’s story into context, describing how, being both Jewish and gay, he felt himself to be a double outsider.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/books/review/27newnoteworthy0/27newnoteworthy0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 295, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/27/books/review/27newnoteworthy0/27newnoteworthy0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 295}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/books/review/27newnoteworthy0/27newnoteworthy0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 443, 'width': 901, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/books/review/27newnoteworthy0/27newnoteworthy0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 443, 'width': 901, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/