e by one to the ground, noticed only by flies? Nope. Black currants, useful only for crème de cassis, and then only if you have a broad definition of “useful”? No, thanks. Honeydews, indestructible totems of hotel breakfast buffets? Not until all the batter at the make-your-own waffle station is gone, and probably not even then.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/23/dining/23fruit/23fruit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/23/dining/23fruit/23fruit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/23/dining/23fruit/23fruit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/23/dining/23fruit/23fruit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/23/dining/23fruit/23fruit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/23/dining/23fruit/23fruit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/23/dining/23fruit/23fruit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The 5 Best Summer Fruits, Ranked', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Season’s Best, Ranked', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fruit', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Watermelons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cherries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Raspberries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Peaches', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blueberries', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-22T18:36:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Wells', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wells', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5e4b7c8-5b0a-5bf4-b7c2-6d222abb540f', 'word_count': 987, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5e4b7c8-5b0a-5bf4-b7c2-6d222abb540f'}, {'abstract': 'Tejal Rao scoured the bottom of the freezer case to come up with this list of her favorite prefabricated pleasures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/22/dining/best-summer-frozen-desserts.html', 'snippet': 'Tejal Rao scoured the bottom of the freezer case to come up with this list of her favorite prefabricated pleasures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I tasted more than 40 individually wrapped bars, bought with cash from the noisy, off-key ice cream trucks that circle my block, as well as the bodegas in my Brooklyn neighborhood. I was looking for big, summery flavors; satisfying, nostalgic textures; and the kind of general resilience that is necessary for a single frozen treat to thrive in a packed chest freezer. I went for everything — novelty character pops, classic sandwiches, ice cream bars co-branded with candy bars.', 'pr