zation': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a034e4b3-587f-5aab-a66c-735cdd9a6548', 'word_count': 1602, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a034e4b3-587f-5aab-a66c-735cdd9a6548'}, {'abstract': 'In “Mirror, Shoulder, Signal,” the Danish novelist Dorthe Nors continues her intense fascination with aging, and with women who have resisted domestication.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/22/books/review-mirror-shoulder-signal-dorthe-nors.html', 'snippet': 'In “Mirror, Shoulder, Signal,” the Danish novelist Dorthe Nors continues her intense fascination with aging, and with women who have resisted domestication.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the few practical pieces of advice I’ve ever received is this: If you want to know if you’re being hustled in chess, ask your opponent to arrange the board. The tell will be in the efficiency of his movements, a kind of unconscious elegance. Virtuosity will out — and always in small, ordinary gestures.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/23/books/23booknors-web/23booknors-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 918, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/23/books/23booknors-web/23booknors-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 918}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/23/books/23booknors-web/23booknors-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 670, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/23/books/23booknors-web/23booknors-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1339, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': '