ter', '_id': 'nyt://article/829ea7ba-722d-58ec-b6f9-7b706c16eb6f', 'word_count': 208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/829ea7ba-722d-58ec-b6f9-7b706c16eb6f'}, {'abstract': 'Peach vs. watermelon. Kielbasa vs. hot dog. Fudgsicle vs. Chipwich. New York Times food critics and writers assess the season’s peak pleasures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/22/dining/best-summer-foods.html', 'snippet': 'Peach vs. watermelon. Kielbasa vs. hot dog. Fudgsicle vs. Chipwich. New York Times food critics and writers assess the season’s peak pleasures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first cool bite off a watermelon wedge. The snap of a hot dog just pulled off the grill. The salty, crisp French fry, dragged through a pool of ketchup. These are the tastes of summer — iconic, indelible, reliably delicious. Our writers and critics have ranked the season’s best (and in some cases, worst), highly subjective lists that assess various summer fruits, types sausages, French fry styles, freezer-case treats and gas-station snacks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/23/dining/23summerlanding-GIF-promo/23summerlanding-GIF-articleLarge.gif', 'height': 443, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/23/dining/23summerlanding-GIF-promo/23summerlanding-GIF-articleLarge.gif', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 443}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/23/dining/23summerlanding-GIF-promo/23summerlanding-GIF-jumbo.gif', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/23/dining/23summerlanding-GIF-promo/23summerlanding-GIF-superJumbo.gif', 'height': 776, 'width': 1050, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo'