ald Trump', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Health Organization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Agency for International Development', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Congo, Democratic Republic of (Congo-Kinshasa)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-22T23:47:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ff9feea-5a6f-5b7a-85a9-cb3cbe61ca7a', 'word_count': 854, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ff9feea-5a6f-5b7a-85a9-cb3cbe61ca7a'}, {'abstract': 'American Indians lived through slavery, the Civil War and white supremacy, just like black and white Americans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/22/opinion/confederate-monuments-indians-original-southerners.html', 'snippet': 'American Indians lived through slavery, the Civil War and white supremacy, just like black and white Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHAPEL HILL, N.C. — The people clamoring over whether to keep or remove Confederate monuments agree on one thing: This is a black-white issue. Last month, a graduate student doused the University of North Carolina’s Confederate monument in a mixture of her own blood and red ink. The monument, she said, “is the genocide of black people.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', '