me': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/27/nyregion/27Misinformed/27Misinformed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/nyregion/27Misinformed/27Misinformed-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'License to Interfere', 'kicker': 'I Was Misinformed', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A License to Interfere Is Liberating', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-23T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joyce Wadler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joyce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wadler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07551374-abd3-5131-9c83-d17e01876044', 'word_count': 1036, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07551374-abd3-5131-9c83-d17e01876044'}, {'abstract': 'Our presidents’ love of detective fiction has an august history. Craig Fehrman follows the clues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/23/books/review/president-mystery-thriller-detective.html', 'snippet': 'Our presidents’ love of detective fiction has an august history. Craig Fehrman follows the clues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Next month will see the publication of “The President Is Missing,” a novel co-written by Bill Clinton and James Patterson. A collaboration between a president and a thriller writer might seem odd. After all, about the only thing their professions have in common is that both lead to books that sell in airports. But “The President Is Missing” belongs to a long tradition of chief executives devouring thrillers, mysteries and detective stories. Clinton isn’t even the first president to participate in the writing of such a book, though this requires some sleuthing to uncover.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/books/review/27Fehrman/27Fehrman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 586, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/27/books/review/27Fehrman/27Fehrman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 586}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/books/review/27Fehrman/27Fehrman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1001, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/books/review/27Fehrman/27Fehrman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1977, 'width': 2023, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/books/review/27Fehrman/27Fehrman-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/27/books/review/27Fehrman/27Fehrman-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/books/review/27Fehrman/27Fehrman-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Mystery Buffs in the White House', 'kicker': 'Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Mystery Buffs in the White House', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Patterson, James', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The President Is Missing (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roosevelt, Franklin Delano', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Poe, Edgar Allan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-23T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Craig Fehrman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Craig', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fehrman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31fa4f82-b5f8-5a73-9cc5-145a25fa6de9', 'word_count': 1440, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31fa4f82-b5f8-5a73-9cc5-145a25fa6de9'}, {'abstract': 'With their political survival at stake in the November midterm elections, frustrated moderates are rising up to demand an immigration vote that they say is long overdue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/23/us/politics/house-republicans-rebellion-immigration.html', 'snippet': 'With their political survival at stake in the November midterm elections, frustrated moderates are rising up to demand an immigration vote that they say is long overdue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Centrist House Republicans have always been like the dependable partner in a turbulent relationship — slightly dull, predictable, the one who remembers family birthdays and pays the bills. It was members of the hard-right caucus who provided the exciting but volatile side, always threatening to break things off unless they got their way.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/24/us/24hulse-print/23hulse_dc-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/24/us/24hulse-print/23hulse_dc-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/24/us/24hulse-print/23hulse_dc-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/24/us/24hulse-print/23hulse_dc-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/24/us/24hulse-print/23hulse_dc-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/24/us/24hulse-print/23hulse_dc-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/24/us/24hulse-print/23hulse_dc-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Usually Reliable and Cooperative, Centrist House Republicans Rebel', 'kicker': 'On Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Weary G.O.P. Bloc Wants Its Way on Immigration', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2018)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deferred Action for Childhood Arrivals', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Curbelo, Carlos (1980- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chamberlain, Sarah', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lance, Leonard', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-23T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Hulse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hulse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a7fe4a2-fd39-5d70-b343-f37004e76258', 'word_count': 1013, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a7fe4a2-fd39-5d70-b343-f37004e76258'}, {'abstract': 'Wherever you are, there’s likely a Bernstein at 100 concert, festival or performance near you. Here are some notable ones, and how to find one close to home.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/23/travel/leonard-bernstein-100-festivals-events.html', 'snippet': 'Wherever you are, there’s likely a Bernstein at 100 concert, festival or performance near you. Here are some notable ones, and how to find one close to home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whether you’re a fan of show tunes, operas or classical music, the name Leonard Bernstein likely rings a familiar melody. The composer, conductor and educator, who died in 1990, would have turned 100 on Aug. 25, and events to commemorate his centennial, collectively called “Leonard Bernstein at 100,” are happening all over the world in 2018, from Vancouver to Vienna.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/travel/27trending-bernstein-1/27trending-bernstein-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 412, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/27/travel/27trending-bernstein-1/27trending-bernstein-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 412}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/travel/27trending-bernstein-1/27trending-bernstein-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/travel/27trending-bernstein-1/27trending-bernstein-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1406, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/travel/27trending-bernstein-1/27trending-bernstein-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/27/travel/27trending-bernstein-1/27trending-bernstein-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/travel/27trending-bernstein-1/27trending-bernstein-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Celebrate 100 Years of Leonard Bernstein With These Festivals', 'kicker': 'Trending', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'So Many Ways to Celebrate a Century of Leonard Bernstein', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernstein, Leonard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-23T09:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b11236ea-ae1b-56db-823e-3a028657d22d', 'word_count': 516, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b11236ea-ae1b-56db-823e-3a028657d22d'}, {'abstract': 'If you’re more Eeyore than Tigger when it comes to sports, reach out and elicit suggestions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/23/well/move/are-you-a-type-d-athlete-relax-and-ask-for-help.html', 'snippet': 'If you’re more Eeyore than Tigger when it comes to sports, reach out and elicit suggestions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Athletes who tend to be anxious, self-doubting and error-prone often undermine themselves, according to a new study of personality and sports performance. But these athletes, who can be described as having a “Type D,” or “distressed,” personality,  might benefit from learning different ways to cope with the stresses of competition, the researchers say. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/29/well/physed-personality/physed-personality-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/29/well/physed-personality/physed-personality-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/29/well/physed-personality/physed-personality-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/29/well/physed-personality/physed-personality-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/29/well/physed-personality/physed-personality-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/29/well/physed-personality/physed-personality-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/29/well/physed-personality/physed-personality-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Are You a ‘Type D’ Athlete? Relax and Ask for Help', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tying Performance to Type', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Winnie-the-Pooh (Fictional Character)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Depression (Mental)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-23T09:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Well', 'subsection_name': 'Move', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Reynolds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reynolds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2ff0803-a9c7-5f41-b50f-6f0828c626f6', 'word_count': 810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2ff0803-a9c7-5f41-b50f-6f0828c626f6'}, {'abstract': 'Now it’s a lodestar amid a mess of bad news, pointing people toward a simple dynamic: Not only did something happen, but also someone is mad about it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/23/magazine/news-of-an-outrage-used-to-mean-something-very-very-different.html', 'snippet': 'Now it’s a lodestar amid a mess of bad news, pointing people toward a simple dynamic: Not only did something happen, but also someone is mad about it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'News celibacy is real. Everyone knows that if you don’t set limits, you’ll find yourself distracted by alert notifications, or looking up the history of Qatar, or wondering if the name Avenatti appears anywhere in Dante’s “The Divine Comedy.” Then there’s the other kind of distraction: some mundane report, putatively meant to keep us informed, that instead induces a sort of acid-reflux reaction, agitating any bilious contempt we’ve already stored for certain people and situations. This reserve, it seems, can be tapped at any minute, triggered by a meme, a sound bite, a headline. And thus we get the thing that’s constantly Ping-Ponging around the news cycle: “outrage.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27FirstWords_01/27FirstWords_01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'cro