 '_id': 'nyt://article/82c5025f-f17f-58c2-8b86-8f87675cf843', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82c5025f-f17f-58c2-8b86-8f87675cf843'}, {'abstract': 'Prime your eyes — have a search image in mind. Consult a tide chart.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/23/magazine/how-to-collect-seashells.html', 'snippet': 'Prime your eyes — have a search image in mind. Consult a tide chart.', 'lead_paragraph': '“It helps to have a search image in your mind,” says José H. Leal, the science director and curator at the Bailey-Matthews National Shell Museum in Florida. Research ahead of time what kind of mollusks you might encounter so that your eyes are primed to pick out specific shapes and colors. Leal has collected seashells since he was a boy in Rio de Janeiro. On his first trip to New York, in his 20s, he was so shell-focused that he dove to the sidewalk before realizing that what he thought were small, unusual clams were actually pistachio shells. “You get fixated,” he says.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27Tip_01-Promo/27Tip_01-articleLarge.png', 'height': 596, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27Tip_01-Promo/27Tip_01-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 596}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27Tip_01-Promo/27Tip_01-jumbo.png', 'height': 1018, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27Tip_01-Promo/27Tip_01-superJumbo.png', 'height': 2036, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail',