trepid reporters have ranked the season’s flavors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/23/dining/the-tastes-of-summer-newsletter.html', 'snippet': 'What’s the season’s best fruit? The finest packaged frozen ice cream? Greatest sausage? Our intrepid reporters have ranked the season’s flavors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. We filled the newspaper we send out to subscribers every morning with lists today: the tastes of summer, ranked. Our restaurant critic, Pete Wells, told us about the season’s best fruit. Julia Moskin, stalwart reporter, evaluated styles of French fry, and Tejal Rao, steadfast chronicler of the ice cream truck business did the same for packaged frozen treats.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/dining/10COOKBOOK3/10COOKBOOK3-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/10/dining/10COOKBOOK3/10COOKBOOK3-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/dining/10COOKBOOK3/10COOKBOOK3-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/dining/10COOKBOOK3/10COOKBOOK3-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/dining/10COOKBOOK3/10COOKBOOK3-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/10/dining/10COOKBOOK3/10COOKBOOK3-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/dining/10COOKBOOK3/10COOKBOOK3-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Tastes of Summer', 'kicker': 'What to Cook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-23T14:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/302b92cd-bf1f-5492-a1b4-a30da87e5b78', 'word_count': 648, 'uri': 'nyt://article/302b92cd-bf1f-5492-a1b4-a30da87e5b78'}, {'abstract': 'When we see it as a fad, separate from the actual deaf people who use it to communicate, we lose sight of the stakes of language.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/23/opinion/sign-language-isnt-just-for-babies.html', 'snippet': 'When we see it as a fad, separate from the actual deaf people who use it to communicate, we lose sight of the stakes of language.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Part of me feels excited whenever hearing acquaintances tell me they’re teaching their infant some baby sign language. (I’m deaf, so I inevitably become a magnet for these conversations.) These parents rave: “It’s so fun and so visual! I can see what my baby is trying to say to me!”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/23/opinion/23Kolb-sub/23Kolb-sub-articleLarge.jp