 government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Internal Revenue Service is preparing to crack down on states that try to circumvent a new limit on the state and local tax deduction, saying on Wednesday that it will not allow local governments to find creative ways to help individuals fully deduct those taxes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I.R.S. Warns States Not to Circumvent State and Local Tax Cap', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I.R.S. Readies Warning For States That Consider Skirting Deduction Cap', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Cuts and Jobs Act (2017)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-23T17:49:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Rappeport and Jim Tankersley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rappeport', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tankersley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9aec6c60-2590-5637-96e3-0f7145097f07', 'word_count': 1268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9aec6c60-2590-5637-96e3-0f7145097f07'}, {'abstract': 'Haifaa al-Mansour sees parallels between her own experience in a conservative society and the life of the 19th-century author of “Frankenstein.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/23/movies/mary-shelley-haifaa-al-mansour-saudi-arabia.html', 'snippet': 'Haifaa al-Mansour sees parallels between her own experience in a conservative society and the life of the 19th-century author of “Frankenstein.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'There were no movie theaters in Saudi Arabia when Haifaa al-Mansour was growing up in Al Hasa, a quiet, conservative town in the Eastern Province, in the 1970s and ’80s. There was a video store, but she wasn’t allowed to enter — only men were. So she stood outside, flipped through a catalog and made selections that a male clerk would take to her. That was how she fell in love with Disney films, Jackie Chan movies and Bollywood musicals, and decided that she wanted to be a filmmaker.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/24/arts/24MARY-SHELLEY-DIRECTOR1/24MARY-SHELLEY-DIRECTOR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 845, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/24/arts/24MARY-SHELLEY-DIRECTOR1/24MARY-SHELLEY-DIRECTOR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 845}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/24/arts/24MARY-SHELLEY-DIRECTOR1/24MARY-SHELLEY-DIRECTOR1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 727, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/24/arts/24MARY-SHELLEY-DIRECTOR1/24MARY-SHELLEY-DIRECTOR1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1454, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/24/arts/24MARY-SHELLEY-DIRECTOR1/24MARY-SHELLEY-DIRECTOR1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 7