'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stephens', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2e4c110-2232-5df6-8eb1-f41c0e37c6dc', 'word_count': 886, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2e4c110-2232-5df6-8eb1-f41c0e37c6dc'}, {'abstract': 'A new federal wage subsidy is a direct way to benefit workers and encourage employment in struggling areas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/24/opinion/heartland-wage-subsidy-rust-belt.html', 'snippet': 'A new federal wage subsidy is a direct way to benefit workers and encourage employment in struggling areas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The national unemployment rate hit 3.9 percent in April, the lowest level since 2000. Still, wage growth has been and remains underwhelming. More alarming, America faces a historic crisis of male joblessness in what we call the Eastern Heartland, a band of states that runs from Louisiana north through to Ohio and Michigan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/23/opinion/23glaeser-summers/23glaeser-summers-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 477, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/23/opinion/23glaeser-summers/23glaeser-summers-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 477}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/23/opinion/23glaeser-summers/23glaeser-summers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 814, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/23/opinion/23glaeser-summers/23glaeser-summers-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1628, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype'