': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/1aabe875-d50c-593c-8665-7c98bfc673ca', 'word_count': 1029, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1aabe875-d50c-593c-8665-7c98bfc673ca'}, {'abstract': '“The least racist person” ever doesn’t bother with dog-whistling. He just lets it all hang out.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/24/opinion/trump-animals-immigrants-politics.html', 'snippet': '“The least racist person” ever doesn’t bother with dog-whistling. He just lets it all hang out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Trump has an almost Apollonian daytime argument in favor of his continued political dominance, which is “Jobs Jobs Jobs!,” “MAGA!” and so forth. He also has a nighttime argument about decline, racial resentment and ethnic hatred. He pushes both strains hard, but the evidence suggests that his heart is really in the hate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/24/opinion/24edsallWeb/merlin_111290786_8307bec2-a068-4c35-953f-c65bd0d87d15-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/24/opinion/24edsallWeb/merlin_111290786_8307bec2-a068-4c35-953f-c65bd0d87d15-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/24/opinion/24edsallWeb/merlin_111290786_8307bec2-a068-4c35-953f-c65bd0d87d15-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/24/opinion/24edsallWeb/merlin_111290786_8307bec2-a068-4c35-953f-c65bd0d87d15-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo',