', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32e85abf-7be6-5659-9d5f-1ef608be094b', 'word_count': 761, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32e85abf-7be6-5659-9d5f-1ef608be094b'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Bateman and an “Arrested Development” co-star, Tony Hale, issued apologies on Thursday after critics said they excused Mr. Tambor’s abusive on-set behavior.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/24/arts/television/arrested-development-jason-bateman-apologizes-jessica-walter-jeffrey-tambor.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Bateman and an “Arrested Development” co-star, Tony Hale, issued apologies on Thursday after critics said they excused Mr. Tambor’s abusive on-set behavior.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Following a blistering reaction on social media, Jason Bateman, one of the stars of “Arrested Development,” apologized on Thursday after an interview with The New York Times during which he defended Jeffrey Tambor, a co-star, and his on-set behavior toward another co-star, Jessica Walter. Critics accused Mr. Bateman of excusing Mr. Tambor’s verbal harassment at the expense of Ms. Walter, during an era in which male toxicity in Hollywood is facing a reckoning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/25/arts/television/25bateman1/merlin_138536979_ac941690-b2a1-4fb1-ab71-1d23ae47908e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/25/arts/television/25bateman1/merlin_138536979_ac941690-b2a1-4fb1-ab71-1d23ae47908e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/25/arts/television/25bateman1/merlin_138536979_ac941690-b2a1-4fb1-ab71-1d23ae47908e-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo