ese are entirely more complex questions, questions hard to answer only by looking at the photograph.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27mag-OnPhoto-image1/27OnPhoto-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27mag-OnPhoto-image1/27OnPhoto-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27mag-OnPhoto-image1/27OnPhoto-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27mag-OnPhoto-image1/27OnPhoto-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27mag-OnPhoto-image1/27OnPhoto-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27mag-OnPhoto-image1/27OnPhoto-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27mag-OnPhoto-image1/27OnPhoto-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Does It Mean to Look at This?', 'kicker': 'On Photography', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Does It Mean to Look at This?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sontag, Susan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meiselas, Susan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ABU GHRAIB (IRAQ)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Regarding the Pain of Others (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-24T15:04:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Teju Cole', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Teju', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cole', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ffb3b9b-978b-5a26-8c8e-c08d085df986', 'word_count': 2225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ffb3b9b-978b-5a26-8c8e-c08d085df986'}, {'abstract': 'Selected by Terrance Hayes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/24/magazine/poem-tamir-rice.html', 'snippet': 'Selected by Terrance Hayes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See the title and brace for heartbreak. See the title and brace for transformational beauty. The speaker, too, is trying to see the title, the name, the answer to the question the daughter asks. You are witness to an intimate scene between parents and their child. Or you are there with the child climbing into your lap. The silence is as tender as the chewed petals of a flower, a wreath. There are no words for the haunting final sentence. Selected by Terrance Hayes', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27Poem/27Poem-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 167, 'width': 338, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/magazine/27Poe