bs1-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1771, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/24/opinion/24Hobbs1/24Hobbs1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/24/opinion/24Hobbs1/24Hobbs1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/24/opinion/24Hobbs1/24Hobbs1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Collateral Damage of a Petty N.F.L.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States National Anthem Protests (2016- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Orleans Saints', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-24T18:59:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Hobbs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hobbs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/657d6285-bf56-59fe-a130-75602e4ef660', 'word_count': 760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/657d6285-bf56-59fe-a130-75602e4ef660'}, {'abstract': 'The fury of having to leave your home to get what you need.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/24/opinion/irish-women-abortion-vote.html', 'snippet': 'The fury of having to leave your home to get what you need.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alison and I became best friends at age 4 after our eyes locked during an intense game of Lego in preschool. We remained obsessed with each other in the important way girls are right up through our teens. She noticed all the same things I did, and we shared everything. It wasn’t My Little Pony; it was Our Little Pony. Well, it was actually a knockoff brand of plastic pony with a shedding glittery mane, but you get my drift. And speaking of drift, that was inevitably what we did throughout our 20s. I left the country and she stayed in our hometown and had her daughters, but still I would know the smell of her house and the sound of her laugh from miles away.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/24/opinion/24higgins/merlin_63265511_310efa05-9703-4a40-9c37-5305c1e2c0b1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/24/opinion/24higgins/merlin_63265511_310efa05-9703-4a40-9c37-5305c1e2c0b1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/24/opinion/24higgins/merlin_63265511_310efa05-9703-4a40-9c37-5305c1e2c0b1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/24/opinion/24higgins/merlin_63265511_310efa05-9703-4a40-9c37-5305c1e2c0b1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/24/opinion/24higgins/24higgins-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/24/opinion/24higgins/24higgins-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/24/opinion/24higgins/24higgins-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Irish Women Know', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ireland', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-24T19:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maeve Higgins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maeve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Higgins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/11e0775f-490a-56d8-a6fc-d623a6e7b6e0', 'word_count': 1357, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11e0775f-490a-56d8-a6fc-d623a6e7b6e0'}, {'abstract': 'Nearly 800,000 New Yorkers would qualify for a discount subway program. Why won’t the mayor put it in his budget proposal?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/24/opinion/mayor-de-blasio-help-new-yorkers-afford-subway-fares.html', 'snippet': 'Nearly 800,000 New Yorkers would qualify for a discount subway program. Why won’t the mayor put it in his budget proposal?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The cost of living in New York City — rent, groceries, health care, mass transit — continues to climb. And the lower your income, the harder these increases hit you. That’s why we’re pushing Mayor Bill de Blasio to adopt Fair Fares, an ambitious, large-scale discount program for subway and bus fares, in his budget proposal for the 2019 fiscal year. It would give half-price MetroCards to working-age New Yorkers living at or below the federal poverty line.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/24/opinion/24Johnson/24Johnson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/24/opinion/24Johnson/24Johnson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/24/opinion/24Johnson/24Johnson-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/24/opinion/24Johnson/24Johnson-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1344, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/24/opinion/24Johnson/24Johnson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/24/opinion/24Johnson/24Johnson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/24/opinion/24Johnson/24Johnson-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mayor de Blasio, Help New Yorkers Afford Subway Fares', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-24T19:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corey Johnson and David R. Jones', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Corey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Jones', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/943d5a00-cfb2-5d36-a648-8695341fa850', 'word_count': 715, 'uri': 'nyt://article/943d5a00-cfb2-5d36-a648-8695341fa850'}, {'abstract': 'I grieve for Alan and for the clarity he brought to the issue of race not just as my husband but as a white man in America.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/24/opinion/sunday/interracial-marriage-trump-mourning.html', 'snippet': 'I grieve for Alan and for the clarity he brought to the issue of race not just as my husband but as a white man in America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I married in 2000, I changed my name. I expanded it — kept my name but added my husband’s name, Kaplan, without a hyphen. I wanted my name to reflect a conjoining that was also an evolution, literally one thing following another. This was an experiment, as all marriages are, that felt exciting and open-ended, not least because I’m black and my husband was white.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 