': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-24T23:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tali Sharot and Cass R. Sunstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tali', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sharot', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Cass', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Sunstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffe2e61e-23e8-55b5-a04e-b322c2c5df08', 'word_count': 796, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffe2e61e-23e8-55b5-a04e-b322c2c5df08'}, {'abstract': 'It’s entertaining! It’s not! Alden Ehrenreich is terrific! He’s no Harrison Ford! The reviews are all over the map, and here’s a sampling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/24/movies/solo-a-star-wars-story-what-do-critics-say-what-do-you-say.html', 'snippet': 'It’s entertaining! It’s not! Alden Ehrenreich is terrific! He’s no Harrison Ford! The reviews are all over the map, and here’s a sampling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like Han Solo himself, the movie about his origins has had its share of ups and downs. There was excitement when Lucasfilm announced “Solo: A Star Wars Story” back in 2015, and fascination when the company said it had hired the “Lego Movie” jokesters, Phil Lord and Christopher Miller, to direct. Then came the stunner, that Mr. Lord and Mr. Miller had been fired well into production, and the news soon after that Ron Howard had been hired to finish the job. (And let’s not even get into fans’ divided reaction to the first trailer and their first look at Alden Ehrenreich in the role that Harrison Ford made famous.)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': N