ionary — but still finds time for pancakes, soccer and “Doctor Who.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In basketball, even LeBron James gets to miss a shot once in a while, but in the cutthroat world of middle-school spelling bees, one mistake can mean you’re out. Rheology? Flittern? Good luck, gentle reader. Neel Iyer, an eighth grader at East Side Middle School in Manhattan, aced these words to grab all-city honors in this year’s Daily News tournament, and will move on to the Scripps National Spelling Bee in Washington, D.C., later this month. It is not a challenge he is taking lightly. “I study 60 pages in the dictionary per day,” Neel, 13, said recently. “I already read through the abridged for the New York City” competition. Eleven million spellers began the competition at the beginning of the school year. Now they are down to 519. For Speller No. 314, Sundays often include attending his younger sister Mira’s soccer games or chorus recitals, about which he only complained a little, really.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/nyregion/27routine1/merlin_137799255_92ebfc00-36c0-4a26-b3cb-8eee82295c16-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/27/nyregion/27routine1/merlin_137799255_92ebfc00-36c0-4a26-b3cb-8eee82295c16-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/nyregion/27routine1/merlin_137799255_92ebfc00-36c0-4a26-b3cb-8eee82295c16-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/nyregion/27routine1/merlin_137799255_92ebfc00-36c0-4a26-b3cb-8eee82295c16-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/nyregion/27routine1/27routine1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/27/nyregion/27routine1/27routine1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/nyregion/27routine1/27routine1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Neel Iyer, Hot-Shot Speller, Spends His Sundays', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When a Spelling Ace Shuts the Dictionary', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Iyer, Neel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spelling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Scripps National Spelling Bee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'East Side Middle School', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-25T09:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Leland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e93bc27-0ea8-5a85-96fb-612ef034b9eb', 'word_count': 650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e93bc27-0ea8-5a85-96fb-612ef034b9eb'}, {'abstract': 'Going to college may increase your income, but higher student debt levels have kept many millennials out of the home buying market.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/25/business/how-student-debt-can-ruin-home-buying-dreams.html', 'snippet': 'Going to college may increase your income, but higher student debt levels have kept many millennials out of the home buying market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Rebecca Wills pictures the home she would like to buy, it looks like the one she grew up in: Small house. Big backyard. Enough grass for the family to lie out on when the New Jersey summers cooperate.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/realestate/27millennials5-SUB/merlin_138611220_67fec02d-08d5-4531-ae54-dc75defefc00-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/27/realestate/27millennials5-SUB/merlin_138611220_67fec02d-08d5-4531-ae54-dc75defefc00-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/realestate/27millennials5-SUB/merlin_138611220_67fec02d-08d5-4531-ae54-dc75defefc00-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/realestate/27millennials5-SUB/merlin_138611220_67fec02d-08d5-4531-ae54-dc75defefc00-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/realestate/27millennials5-SUB/27millennials5-SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width