77d-5378-8282-4cfe940c62b8'}, {'abstract': 'The authors up for the one-time award include Hilary Mantel, V.S. Naipaul and Michael Ondaatje.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/26/books/5-novels-golden-booker-prize.html', 'snippet': 'The authors up for the one-time award include Hilary Mantel, V.S. Naipaul and Michael Ondaatje.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Five novels, including “The English Patient” and “Wolf Hall,” have been named to a short list of former Man Booker Prize winners eligible for a special award to commemorate the 50th anniversary of the prize.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '5 Novels Selected To Vie as Best of the Booker Prize Winners', 'kicker': 'Books News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Special Booker Prize Has Five Contenders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Man Booker Prize', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-26T17:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Libbey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Libbey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfd5fa06-0bb2-5c05-a13b-a8c52bae36a4', 'word_count': 333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfd5fa06-0bb2-5c05-a13b-a8c52bae36a4'}, {'abstract': 'The institution may be in decline. But Ireland has not simply transformed into another secular Western European country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/26/opinion/ireland-catholic-abortion-referendum.html', 'snippet': 'The institution may be in decline. But Ireland has not simply transformed into another secular Western European country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DUBLIN — Shortly before he died in 1989, the novelist John Broderick was asked by an interviewer what it meant to be Roman Catholic and Irish. “Anyone who is reared in a Catholic atmosphere,” he replied, “takes in that Catholic atmosphere more or less through their pores.” That we are a few decades removed from 1989 is clear enough. It became more so on Friday, when Ireland voted resoundingly to overturn its 35-year-old constitutional ban on abortion. And yet it takes more than one vote, or even two or three, to reverse that kind of osmosis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/26/opinion/26maher/merlin_128347259_3d25a5da-298c-4867-b944-0b1732d012e2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/26/opinion/26maher/merlin_128347259_3d25a5da-298c-4867-b944-0b1732d012e2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/26/opinion/26maher/merlin_128347259_3d25a5da-298c-4867-b944-0b1732d012e2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/26/opinion/26maher/merlin_128347259_3d25a5da-298c-4867-b944-0b1732d012e2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/26/opinion/26maher/26maher-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/26/opinion/26maher/26maher-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', '