rs in Iraq and Afghanistan, I represented the State Department in the battleground regions of Falluja and Helmand Province. Like many of the service members I served alongside, I had courageous American friends die in combat. But those troops are not the only dead I remember each Memorial Day.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/sunday-review/27weston/27weston-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/27/sunday-review/27weston/27weston-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/sunday-review/27weston/27weston-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/sunday-review/27weston/27weston-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1371, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/sunday-review/27weston/27weston-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/27/sunday-review/27weston/27weston-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/sunday-review/27weston/27weston-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Other Names We Must Not Forget', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Other Names We Must Not Forget', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nicholson, John W Jr (1957- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANBAR PROVINCE (IRAQ)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Helmand Province (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Memorial Day', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-26T18:32:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. Kael Weston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'Kael', 'lastname': 'Weston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ae64b89-32bd-5fc5-8f0e-2103905a5a12', 'word_count': 901, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ae64b89-32bd-5fc5-8f0e-2103905a5a12'}, {'abstract': 'Despite declining enrollment, traditional college majors are more important than ever.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/26/opinion/sunday/college-majors-liberal-arts.html', 'snippet': 'Despite declining enrollment, traditional college majors are more important than ever.', 'lead_paragraph': ' History is on the ebb. Philosophy is on the ropes. And comparative literature? Please. It’s an intellectual heirloom: cherished by those who can afford such baubles but disposable in the eyes of others.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/27/opinion/sunday/2