o find out how they approached the second to last installment in a series.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Avengers: Infinity War” is still going strong a month after it opened, even though its whopper of a cliffhanger ending continues to divide audiences. The final chapter of the film isn’t set to hit theaters until May 2019, and the filmmakers faced a task familiar to writers of franchises going back to “Star Wars”: How do you plot out the penultimate film in a series so that you both satisfy audiences of the current film and make them want to return for more?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/28/arts/28trilogy-screenwriters1/merlin_136943883_5ec36206-8926-4a78-95b6-0eae4125d6d7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 317, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/28/arts/28trilogy-screenwriters1/merlin_136943883_5ec36206-8926-4a78-95b6-0eae4125d6d7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 317}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/28/arts/28trilogy-screenwriters1/merlin_136943883_5ec36206-8926-4a78-95b6-0eae4125d6d7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 540, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/28/arts/28trilogy-screenwriters1/merlin_136943883_5ec36206-8926-4a78-95b6-0eae4125d6d7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 2047, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/28/arts/28trilogy-screenwriters1/28trilogy-screenwriters1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 