more cutting-edge drugs. But the agency says its mission doesn’t include evaluating prices, even when the drugs use breakthroughs it patented.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — On Aug. 30, the Food and Drug Administration approved a radical new cancer treatment that harnesses a patient’s immune system to attack tumor cells. The drug, known as Kymriah, grew out of research conducted and supported by the National Institutes of Health.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/25/us/00dc-health-1/merlin_126580937_3e230114-6c7e-4060-a59d-bb3e25cf2fc8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/25/us/00dc-health-1/merlin_126580937_3e230114-6c7e-4060-a59d-bb3e25cf2fc8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/25/us/00dc-health-1/merlin_126580937_3e230114-6c7e-4060-a59d-bb3e25cf2fc8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/25/us/00dc-health-1/merlin_126580937_3e230114-6c7e-4060-a59d-bb3e25cf2fc8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/25/us/00dc-health-1/merlin_126580937_3e230114-6c7e-4060-a59d-bb3e25cf2fc8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/25/us/00dc-health-1/merlin_126580937_3e230114-6c7e-4060-a59d-bb3e25cf2fc8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thu