nst allies, ignoring real threats from dictatorships.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/28/opinion/trump-china-trade-policy.html', 'snippet': 'Using phony national security arguments against allies, ignoring real threats from dictatorships.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Remember “The Manchurian Candidate”? The 1959 novel, made into a classic 1962 film (never mind the remake), involved a plot to install a Communist agent as president of the United States. One major irony was that the politician in question was modeled on Senator Joe McCarthy — that is, he posed as a superpatriot even while planning to betray America.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/28/opinion/28krugmanWeb/28krugmanWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 361, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/28/opinion/28krugmanWeb/28krugmanWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 361}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/28/opinion/28krugmanWeb/28krugmanWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 617, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/28/opinion/28krugmanWeb/28krugmanWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1234, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/28/opinion/28krugmanWeb/28krugmanWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/28/opinion/28krugmanWeb/28krugmanWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0,