me to sleep. This is legal in my state, and I have gone through appropriate channels to purchase tablets at an approved dispensary.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/06/03/magazine/03mag-ethicist-image1/03mag-03ethicist-t_CA0-jumbo.png', 'height': 736, 'width': 496, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/06/03/magazine/03mag-ethicist-image1/03mag-03ethicist-t_CA0-superJumbo.png', 'height': 736, 'width': 496, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/06/03/magazine/03mag-ethicist-image1/03mag-03ethicist-t_CA0-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/06/03/magazine/03mag-ethicist-image1/03mag-03ethicist-t_CA0-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/06/03/magazine/03mag-ethicist-image1/03mag-03ethicist-t_CA0-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Should I Tell My Hosts About My Medical Marijuana?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Should I Tell My Hosts About My Medical Marijuana?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medical Marijuana', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dementia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-29T09:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kwame Anthony Appiah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kwame', 'middlename': 'Anthony', 'lastname': 'Appiah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe10211e-2827-5a52-a6f8-657348006b56', 'word_count': 1175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe10211e-2827-5a52-a6f8-657348006b56'}, {'abstract': 'With its new exhibit, “Black Women: Power and Grace,” the African-American photography collective Kamoinge presents a mosaic of identity, history and little-seen stories.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/29/lens/celebrating-the-grace-of-black-women.html', 'snippet': 'With its new exhibit, “Black Women: Power and Grace,” the African-American photography collective Kamoinge presents a mosaic of identity, history and little-seen stories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than half a century after the groundbreaking exhibit “The Negro Woman,” the image announcing the show by the African-American collective Kamoinge still captivates. Taken by Louis Draper, who had a keen sense of light and shadow, the photograph shows an older black woman standing on a busy Harlem street corner. In the crowd, her face is finely in focus. She is tired, gazing off into the distance, as she waits, with serious dignity and grace. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/29/lens/29kamoinge1/29kamoinge1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/29/lens/29kamoinge1/29kamoinge1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/201