: 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Omorovicza Cosmetics Limited', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-29T15:59:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kari Molvar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Molvar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec72da80-0aaf-5901-b0e3-0abc33c5223d', 'word_count': 686, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec72da80-0aaf-5901-b0e3-0abc33c5223d'}, {'abstract': 'Community health workers who used to be locked up themselves are helping recently released inmates get care for mental illness, addiction and other health problems.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/29/health/ex-prisoners-health-california.html', 'snippet': 'Community health workers who used to be locked up themselves are helping recently released inmates get care for mental illness, addiction and other health problems.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — The night Ronald Sanders turned his life around, he had been smoking crack for two days in a tiny, airless room. His infant son, Isaiah, was breathing in the fumes. “His chest was beating really hard,” Mr. Sanders recalled. “So I pray: ‘If my son makes it through the night, that’s it.’”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/science/00EXPRISONERS1/00EXPRISONERS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/21/science/00EXPRISONERS1/00EXPRISONERS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/science/00EXPRISONERS1/00EXPRISONERS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/science/00EXPRISONERS1/00EXPRISONERS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/science/00EXPRISONERS1/00EXPRISONERS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/21/science/00EXPRISONERS1/00EXPRISONERS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/21/science/00EXPRISONERS1/00EXPRISONERS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'They’re Out of Prison. Can They Stay Out of the Hospital?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Health Care Program for Ex-Inmates by Ex-Inmates', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ex-Convicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transitions Clinic Network', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-29T16:01:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Leigh Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': 'Leigh', 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/160a1c3d-1302-5cf8-9f83-a1e28ee2c8be', 'word_count': 1385, 'uri': 'nyt://article/160a1c3d-1302-5cf8-9f83-a1e28ee2c8be'}, {'abstract': 'Ink Gourmet makes the condiments in six flavors, including orange-chile and wasabi.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/29/dining/ink-gourmet-soy-sauce.html', 'snippet': 'Ink Gourmet makes the condiments in six flavors, including orange-chile and wasabi.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You can find both regular or low-sodium soy sauce, with or without wheat. Now, Ink Gourmet, a company based in Mesquite, Tex., sells it in six flavors. The orange-chile version, thicker than regular Chinese soy sauce, is meant to turn that simple stir-fry into the popular orange chicken or beef. Wasabi, lemongrass and Thai chile are some other options: $10.99 for eight ounces, lower prices for several bottles, inksoysauce.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/dining/30burnersoy/30burnersoy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 490, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/30/dining/30burnersoy/30burnersoy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 490}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/dining/30burnersoy/30burnersoy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 837, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/dining/30burnersoy/30burnersoy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1673, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/dining/30burnersoy/30burnersoy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/30/dining/30burnersoy/30burnersoy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/dining/30burnersoy/30burnersoy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Soy Sauces With Texas-Size Flavors', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Season: Texas-Size Flavors Suited for Stir-Fry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Condiments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soy Sauce', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-29T16:02:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1db64a95-9271-51de-ae31-091542a1f3eb', 'word_count': 92, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1db64a95-9271-51de-ae31-091542a1f3eb'}, {'abstract': 'A resource helps consumers navigate labels on about 150 brands of eggs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/29/dining/organic-egg-ratings-cornucopia-institute.html', 'snippet': 'A resource helps consumers navigate labels on about 150 brands of eggs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s worth studying the many shades of organic, especially regarding eggs. The organic label can be slapped onto cartons of eggs laid by hens crowded in semiconfinement on megafarms, as well as on those from hens that scratch outdoors for dinner. The Cornucopia Institute, a nonprofit agricultural watchdog group that reveals industrial practices within the elastic organic standards, began rating eggs over five years ago. The ratings, updated last year, are based on how the birds are raised. About 150 local and national brands are judged at one to five eggs, the highest mark. The organization does not have an app yet, but Mark Kastel, a founder, said the online chart is mobile friendly. Yogurt and other dairy products, pet foods and more have also been evaluated on the website: cornucopia.org.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/dining/30burneregg/30burneregg-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 281, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/30/dining/30burneregg/30burneregg-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 281}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/dining/30burneregg/30burneregg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/dining/30burneregg/30burneregg-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 960, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/dining/30burneregg/30burneregg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/30/dining/30burneregg/30burneregg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/dining/30burneregg/30burneregg-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Organic Egg Ratings at Your Fingertips', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Evaluate: A Handy Ratings Guide For Eggs Labeled Organic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eggs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-29T16:10:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bdf50b75-c982-502e-a209-f0528d78002d', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bdf50b75-c982-502e-a209-f0528d78002d'}, {'abstract': 'For some people, car services like Uber and Via provide more than just transportation. They turn out to be vehicles for meeting their beloved. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/29/style/one-door-closes-and-an-uber-door-opens-love-follows.html', 'snippet': 'For some people, car services like Uber and Via provide more than just transportation. They turn out to be vehicles for meeting their beloved. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fourteen minutes and 35 seconds. That’s how long it took Ed Santos and Jill Sciuto’s futures to radically alter course. Less than 15 minutes. A car ride from Manhattan to Brooklyn.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/22/fashion/weddings/22uber/22uber-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 412, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/22/fashion/weddings/22uber/22uber-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 412}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/22/fashion/weddings/22uber/22uber-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/22/fashion/weddings/22uber/22uber-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/22/fashion/weddings/22uber/22uber-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/22/fashion/weddings/22uber/22uber-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/22/fashion/weddings/22uber/22uber-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One Door Closes, and an Uber Door Opens. Love Follows.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Car Services and Livery Cabs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Relationships', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Uber Technologies Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Via Transportation Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-29T16:12:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Ellin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ellin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2641828c-6cc9-5222-9d90-656eb138e01f', 'word_count': 2642, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2641828c-6cc9-5222-9d90-656eb138e01f'}, {'abstract': 'A group led by Wolfgang Tillmans and Rem Koolhaas is discussing how the organization can “be recognized as a force for good, rather than as a faceless bureaucracy.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/29/arts/design/europe-rebranding-wolfgang-tillmans-rem-koolhaas.html', 'snippet': 'A group led by Wolfgang Tillmans and Rem Koolhaas is discussing how the organization can “be recognized as a force for good, rather than as a faceless bureaucracy.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'AMSTERDAM — With populist politicians across the Continent attacking the European Union and negotiations underway for Britain to leave the bloc, the very idea of a unified Europe seems to be under threat. Some artists feel the union needs to rethink its public image and refine its communications strategy to combat these attacks. In other words: to rebrand Europe.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/arts/30rebranding1/30rebranding1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/30/arts/30rebranding1/30rebranding1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'