': 'Siegal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fecb6f70-bc93-53b9-a0d1-f23e6acfbad9', 'word_count': 864, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fecb6f70-bc93-53b9-a0d1-f23e6acfbad9'}, {'abstract': 'Alexei Ratmansky is restaging Marius Petipa’s ballet not by patching together known versions, but by going to back to a written source.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/29/arts/dance/harlequinade-alexei-ratmansky-american-ballet-theater.html', 'snippet': 'Alexei Ratmansky is restaging Marius Petipa’s ballet not by patching together known versions, but by going to back to a written source.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We think of ballet as a nonverbal art, but for the last few months, the words “tell” and “say” have echoed in the studios of American Ballet Theater. The dancers aren’t using their voices; it is their bodies that are doing the talking.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/arts/30HARLEQUINADE1/merlin_138678648_b107e75e-2163-4696-8d88-6e193773df08-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/30/arts/30HARLEQUINADE1/merlin_138678648_b107e75e-2163-4696-8d88-6e193773df08-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/arts/30HARLEQUINADE1/merlin_138678648_b107e75e-2163-4696-8d88-6e193773df08-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/arts/30HARLEQUINADE1/merlin_138678648_b107e75e-2163-4696-8d88-6e193773df08-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/arts/30HARLEQUINADE1/30HARLEQUINADE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/30/arts/30HARLEQUINADE1/30HARLEQUINADE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/arts/30HARLEQUINADE1/30HARLEQUINADE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In ‘Harlequinade,’ Gestures Dance, and Dances Tell Stories', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A ballet of gestures, redone by research', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN BALLET THEATER', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Petipa, Marius', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ratmansky, Alexei', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Harlequinade (Ballet)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-29T16:20:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marina Harss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa149904-921d-5f52-ab22-1946d1495dc9', 'word_count': 1120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa149904-921d-5f52-ab22-1946d1495dc9'}, {'abstract': 'Btarts, a new pastry company based in Brooklyn, ships the sugary Canadian treat nationwide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/29/dining/butter-tarts-btarts-smorgasburg.html', 'snippet': 'Btarts, a new pastry company based in Brooklyn, ships the sugary Canadian treat nationwide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Butter tarts are to Canada what natas are to Portugal, mellow little dessert pastries sold and served everywhere. In Canada, a flaky tart shell holds a dense, sweet sugar custard not unlike pecan pie filling. Longing for butter tarts after moving to the United States from Toronto, Asher Weiss adapted his great-grandmother’s recipe and is producing them in Brooklyn. They’re sold at Smorgasburg and nationwide: Btarts, $5 each, $27 for six at Smorgasburg, $59 for six online (includes shipping), $89 for 12, eatbtarts.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/dining/30burnertarts/30burnertarts-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/30/dining/30burnertarts/30burnertarts-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/dining/30burnertarts/30burnertarts-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/dining/30burnertarts/30burnertarts-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/dining/30burnertarts/30burnertarts-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbSt