brick building that stood empty for some time. It will open in stages, through Monday, with a score of food stands. Many of them, like Di Fara Pizza, Corner Bistro for burgers, and Harvest2Order, where microgreens are grown and freshly cut for salads and bowls, are, for the first time, opening in a food hall. Bien Cuit bakery, Chuko for ramen, La Newyorkina for Mexican confections, Dana’s Bakery for macaroons, Baba’s Pierogies and Chris Cheung’s East Wind Snack Shop, are some of the other spots to open in the food hall. Mrktpl, the company owned by Manny Del Castillo and Jamie Hinojos that developed the market with Leny, the building’s owner, has also invested in the art scene, with local talent creating work for the space. Eventually, there will be a catering hall in the back: 103 North Third Street (Berry Street), Williamsburg, Brooklyn, north3rdstreetmarket.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/dining/30off/30off-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/30/dining/30off/30off-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/dining/30off/30off-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/dining/30off/30off-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/dining/30off/30off-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name