esponded to Roseanne Barr’s firing after a controversial tweet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Roseanne Barr unleashed a tweetstorm that included a racist post against Valerie Jarrett, who was a senior adviser to President Obama, Twitter was filled with impassioned responses, many coming from high-profile users. The conversation only grew louder once ABC announced it had fired Ms. Barr and canceled the next season of her sitcom, “Roseanne.” While some defended her, many condemned her words and applauded ABC for its decision.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/arts/30roseanne-reax3/merlin_136344087_799861a5-1a1c-44a0-86f1-3dc4ae71389a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/30/arts/30roseanne-reax3/merlin_136344087_799861a5-1a1c-44a0-86f1-3dc4ae71389a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/arts/30roseanne-reax3/merlin_136344087_799861a5-1a1c-44a0-86f1-3dc4ae71389a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 664, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/arts/30roseanne-reax3/merlin_136344087_799861a5-1a1c-44a0-86f1-3dc4ae71389a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1329, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/arts/30roseanne-reax3/30roseanne-reax3-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/30/arts/30roseanne-reax3/30roseanne-reax3-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 7