iser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/670ed54e-0eff-56b4-b87f-396547505f5b', 'word_count': 1224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/670ed54e-0eff-56b4-b87f-396547505f5b'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Barr has a history of insensitive tweets as well as those that endorse fringe conspiracy theories. Here are some of them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/29/arts/television/twitter-posts-roseanne-barr.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Barr has a history of insensitive tweets as well as those that endorse fringe conspiracy theories. Here are some of them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Roseanne Barr found herself at the center of a firestorm on Tuesday, after a racist post on her Twitter account compared Valerie Jarrett, an African-American and a former special adviser to former President Barack Obama, to an ape. Her show, “Roseanne,” which had been a ratings hit when it was revived this spring, was swiftly canceled by ABC, scrapping plans for what would have been its 11th season over all.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/arts/30roseanne-tweets/merlin_138827994_a5d8c9a6-78cd-44b6-9e0e-2883ccf3659f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/30/arts/30roseanne-tweets/merlin_138827994_a5d8c9a6-78cd-44b6-9e0e-2883ccf3659f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/arts/30roseanne-tweets/merlin_138827994_a5d8c9a6-78cd-44b6-9e0e-2883ccf3659f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/201