ojects.html', 'snippet': 'The decision to nationalize the Trans Mountain pipeline underscores the country’s growing ambivalence about fossil fuels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While living in Calgary, the headquarters of Canada’s oil and gas industry, I occasionally heard people in the business say their pipelines were cursed. The country was brimming with oil and gas, and yet battles over proposed pipelines had limited the ability of producers to get those resources to market.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/opinion/sunday/30Kujawinski/merlin_138823902_161774d0-ce3c-4d22-a188-5495ea965729-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/30/opinion/sunday/30Kujawinski/merlin_138823902_161774d0-ce3c-4d22-a188-5495ea965729-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/opinion/sunday/30Kujawinski/merlin_138823902_161774d0-ce3c-4d22-a188-5495ea965729-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/opinion/sunday/30Kujawinski/merlin_138823902_161774d0-ce3c-4d22-a188-5495ea965729-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1384, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/30/opinion/sunday/30Kujawinski/30Kujawinski-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/30/opinion/sunday/30Kujawinski/30Kujawinski-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}