 are hired on looks and dressed like cheerleaders, but their primary job is to charm the team’s fans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/31/sports/nfl-cheerleaders.html', 'snippet': 'Noncheering cheerleaders are hired on looks and dressed like cheerleaders, but their primary job is to charm the team’s fans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Several N.F.L. teams determined cheerleading programs had a scarcity problem on game days. If cheerleaders were on the sideline dancing, none were available to serve as scantily clad hostesses who could mingle with fans high up in the cheap seats or in the luxury suites, where teams catered to big-money customers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/26/sports/26cheer-web1/merlin_138563202_d7bfb174-163a-4203-8db4-f472a71957dd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/26/sports/26cheer-web1/merlin_138563202_d7bfb174-163a-4203-8db4-f472a71957dd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/26/sports/26cheer-web1/merlin_138563202_d7bfb174-163a-4203-8db4-f472a71957dd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/26/sports/26cheer-web1/merlin_138563202_d7bfb174-163a-4203-8db4-f472a71957dd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/26/sports/26cheer-web1/26cheer-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/26/sports/26cheer-web1/26cheer-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/26/sports/26cheer-web1/26cheer-web1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'N.F.L.’s Alternate ‘Cheerleaders’ Don’t Cheer or Dance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'They Wear the Uniform, but They Don’t Cheer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheerleaders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houston Texans', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Redskins', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-31T09:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Macur', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macur', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d803b2ad-2a63-5dab-a695-a5e5d48dd5a3', 'word_count': 2112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d803b2ad-2a63-5dab-a695-a5e5d48dd5a3'}, {'abstract': 'The yellow warbler is perfectly named. It’s also harsh as a parent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/31/nyregion/beautiful-and-brutal.html', 'snippet': 'The yellow warbler is perfectly named. It’s also harsh as a parent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Spring came reluctantly to New York City this year. Delayed by an uncooperative March, which refused to go out like a lamb, it was followed by an April so complicit, the leonine weather continued through May. The first migrant birds seemed to arrive hesitatingly and late, alighting on frost-damaged blooms with cold feet. But persevering, the waves of migrants finally arrived, shining briefly on sun-warmed, leafy branches. But after its fleeting stay, restless spring is moving northward.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/06/03/nyregion/03NATURE/03NATURE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/06/03/nyregion/03NATURE/03NATURE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 387}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/06/03/nyregion/03NATURE/03NATURE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/06/03/nyregion/03NATURE/03NATURE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1291, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/06/03/nyregion/03NATURE/03NATURE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/06/03/nyregion/03NATURE/03NATURE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/06/03/nyregion/03NATURE/03NATURE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Beautiful and Brutal', 'kicker': 'N.Y.C. Nature', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beautiful and Brazen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birdwatching', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-31T09:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Taft', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taft', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6fe1a75-fafa-51e5-aac3-5d6dfc2137db', 'word_count': 543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6fe1a75-fafa-51e5-aac3-5d6dfc2137db'}, {'abstract': 'A lesson in how partisan polarization colors people’s views on a gut emotional level without many even realizing it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/31/upshot/liberals-immigration-children-border-misinformation.html', 'snippet': 'A lesson in how partisan polarization colors people’s views on a gut emotional level without many even realizing it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the weekend, you may have seen a horrifying story: Almost 1,500 migrant children were missing, and feared to be in the hands of human traffickers. The Trump administration lost track of the children, the story went, after separating them from their parents at the border.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/31/upshot/up-fake/merlin_138808566_f368ad96-3610-421e-a4ae-fff0bff42e4c-articleLarge.jpg', 'hei