er for a decade when William E. Crawford arrived in Hanoi with a group of filmmakers and veterans in 1985, tensions persisted. The American trade embargo of Vietnam continued, the fate of missing American servicemen remained an emotionally charged question, and the United States was still demanding that Vietnam withdraw its troops from Cambodia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/06/01/lens/31-lens-hanoi1/31-lens-hanoi1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 605, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/06/01/lens/31-lens-hanoi1/31-lens-hanoi1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 605}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/06/01/lens/31-lens-hanoi1/31-lens-hanoi1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1015, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/06/01/lens/31-lens-hanoi1/31-lens-hanoi1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2030, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/06/01/lens/31-lens-hanoi1/31-lens-hanoi1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/06/01/lens/31-lens-hanoi1/31-lens-hanoi1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/06/01/lens/31-lens-hanoi1/31-lens-hanoi1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Documenting Hanoi’s Postwar Evolution ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hanoi (Vietnam)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crawford, William E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vietnam War', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-05-31T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NYTNow', 'section_name': 'Lens', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jordan G. Teicher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jordan', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Teicher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/844c2498-3897-5f18-a669-b108a7b0a548', 'word_count': 661, 'uri': 'nyt://article/844c2498-3897-5f18-a669-b108a7b0a548'}, {'abstract': 'In a survey, nearly three in four American adults said teachers’ salaries were too low. The sentiment crossed party lines, even if raises meant higher taxes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/31/us/politics/teachers-campaign.html', 'snippet': 'In a survey, nearly three in four American adults said teachers’ salaries were too low. The sentiment crossed party lines, even if raises meant higher taxes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After shutting down schools and shaking up politics in six states, teachers are looking to the ballot box in their campaign for better pay and increased school funding. And their demands are meeting with widespread public support.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/06/01/business/01teacherpoll-1-print/01teacherpoll-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/06/01/bus