nytimes.com/2018/05/31/magazine/syria-conflict-manbij.html', 'snippet': 'Kurdish fighters and Manbij residents reflect on life in a Syrian hot spot, where the geopolitics of the conflict are in plain view.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About six miles north of the Syrian city Manbij is a town near the Turkish border called Dadat, which has been ruled by multiple occupiers since 2012. Atop one hill, the armed fighters of the predominantly Kurdish Syrian Democratic Forces, or S.D.F., crouch within bunkers and behind earthen walls. Through binoculars they stare at their enemies: the Turkish Army and Turkish-backed Syrian militias, who have built their own bases and bunkers about a mile away.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/31/magazine/31SYRIA/merlin_136324368_510900a8-59e3-41a8-9142-aec46452370a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/31/magazine/31SYRIA/merlin_136324368_510900a8-59e3-41a8-9142-aec46452370a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/31/magazine/31SYRIA/merlin_136324368_510900a8-59e3-41a8-9142-aec46452370a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/31/magazine/31SYRIA/merlin_136324368_510900a8-59e3-41a8-9142-aec46452370a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1359, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/31/magazine/31SYRIA/merlin_136324368_510900a8-59e3-41a8-9142-aec46452370a-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'sub