', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zhong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d086d155-4f9b-57db-b725-b9d9d1cf8002', 'word_count': 1273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d086d155-4f9b-57db-b725-b9d9d1cf8002'}, {'abstract': 'About 50 officers still carry the storied six-shot revolver that became the standard department firearm in 1895, but the weapon is being phased out.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/05/31/nyregion/new-york-police-revolver.html', 'snippet': 'About 50 officers still carry the storied six-shot revolver that became the standard department firearm in 1895, but the weapon is being phased out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Plenty of things have changed about the New York Police Department since Lt. James Darcy joined in 1987. Until now, the service weapon swinging at his hip, a .38-caliber Ruger Service-Six, has not been one of them.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/06/01/nyregion/01revolver-promo/01revolver-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/06/01/nyregion/01revolver-promo/01revolver-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/06/01/nyregion/01revolver-promo/01revolver-promo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/06/01/nyregion/01revolver-promo/01revolver-promo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subty